My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T03:51:11-07:00","id":1112589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1112583#post1112583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Apocalypse already gave us one take on Wild West Werewolves. Let someone else have some fun with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>We did get Viking Forsaken when there were Viking Apocalypse books ( Dark Age WtA books). But even then, Apocalypse is <i>totally</i> different beast than Forsaken in running, especially in historical chronicles. I would really love to see Westerners and Natives Uratha fight over territory - or even how Tribes are reflected in Native Americans culture. It's not simple 'Natives tribe A is Moon Tribe 1', etc. This is one of largest difference between <b>WtA</b> and <b>WtF</b> - there is no 'all of our Kin are Wendigo' kind of thing. On the other hand - Tribes in WtF <i>are</i> connected to specific cultures, somehow ( see Forsaken by Rome for understanding concept ).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1112583#post1112583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rails are absolutely the most perfect representation of the God-Machine in human history.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that Cold War Intelligence Agencies are much better as G-M Infrastructure, that's why I was all for Cold War DtD. <b>Beside, what would Demons do in times of Wild West, beside bombarding railroads industry?</b><br /> <br /> <b>Werewolves in that time can hunt Shadow Realm flora &amp; fauna, makes deal with Natives American and their literal Totems, being normal humans bonty hunters just to satisfied their crave for Hunt - or try to please this new spirit beasts called 'trains'.</b> And I only starting here. Wild West <i>really</i> should be Werewolf in it's half.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1112588#post1112588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the main reason that I don't find the Wold West Geist/Werewolf as interesting is that we already have two Eras which combine those splats. Doing too many Crossover Eras with the same Crossover is just lazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, you do not want Geist for crossover? Let's get Mage then and let me see this all Nameless shamans, Awakened anarchists obstructing new territories with their railroad or how Adamantine Arrows become something more than hired gun on the West. Add some really weird places of Time Before - and we are golden! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-07-2017, 07:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T04:12:44-07:00","id":1112593,"title":"","content":"I would love to see wild west werewolves and also demon or geist","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T04:29:22-07:00","id":1112594,"title":"","content":"Geist aside, which I do agree would be cool for the Wild West, my other actual suggestion for it would be Promethean.<br /> <br /> Picture this: a lone figure arrives into town. Inevitably, trouble follows him, as tensions rise and people fight. The stranger is forced into fight and, when dust settles, he leaves, knowing that its presence would harm the community and put others into danger.<br /> <br /> That's pretty much the most classic, blatant and lazy way to write a Western or a Promethean, but it's an example of how the genres align. You'd also have things like Firestorms over endless plains, Pandorans rising from the dust, &quot;angels&quot; that exalt chosen ones and Promethean both made of steam and magic. Plus, wanderers, Lots of wanderers.<br /> <br /> I could keep going forever; you can take pretty much all Western movies and translate them to Promethean more easily than to other lines. I do think Wild West Geist should be a thing, because Western folklore about the dead is awesomely weird, but it's Promethean I hope the most for it. Demon...well, the rise of railroads and mechanization of the frontier does have plenty of good story hooks for it. Robot cowboys and gears buried in the desert. Cool.<br /> <br /> As someone who loves the Western genre and also likes the WoD (and Werewolf being my favorite along with Old Demon), I got tons of mileage of out Apocalypse Wild West and, while it's true the settings are really different, I do think it would be better to not go there for Forsaken. There are some shared elements between them which make me think having Forsaken Wild West might be a waste of potential. Don't get me wrong, I can live with it if that happens, but we have so many completely unexplored option to choose from.<br /> <br /> Either Promethean/Geist or Promethean/Demon are options I'd love for the Era.<br /> <br /> Assuming the usual suspects don't win the hypothetical votation. Again and again and again (sorry, having flashbacks of Dark Eras 1 where the things I hoped for almost always got second. I mean, there's a real risk we won't have Pirate Geist, at this point. What the hell people, you're gonna make me cry)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 07-07-2017, 07:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T04:29:42-07:00","id":1112595,"title":"","content":"In place of Geist or Mage I would pointed Promethean for Wild West - but I would feel it would look more or like <i>Handfull of Dust</i>, only 50-100 years earlier - you know, Created traveling dusty towns and making some temporary work, until Disquiet in community lead them to leave. But hey, hard work on putting railroad is EXACTLY like this! EDIT: Cinder ninjed me on this idea and arguments. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-07-2017, 07:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T04:41:46-07:00","id":1112598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1112594#post1112594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming the usual suspects don't win the hypothetical votation. Again and again and again (sorry, having flashbacks of Dark Eras 1 where the things I hoped for almost always got second. I mean, there's a real risk we won't have Pirate Geist, at this point. What the hell people, you're gonna make me cry)</div> </div> </div> </div>To be frank, it looks like Demon is on the rise on Pirate Dark Era - from some weird reason, I must say. Even if I do not like he took up place from Mage or Beast on French Revolution - it at least have <i>some</i> sense in great revolt times. But what could Demon give to Pirates? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm really puzzled and concerned on this trend...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T04:55:57-07:00","id":1112601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1112598#post1112598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be frank, it looks like Demon is on the rise on Pirate Dark Era - from some weird reason, I must say. Even if I do not like he took up place from Mage or Beast on French Revolution - it at least have <i>some</i> sense in great revolt times. But what could Demon give to Pirates? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm really puzzled and concerned on this trend...</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh, I'll be honest. On one hand, having gamelines that don't look like the perfect fit can provide innovative and unexpected takes on a certain Dark Era. That's why I generally say I can roll with whatever we get.<br /> <br /> But, on the other hand, sometimes a perfect fit is just that: perfect.<br /> <br /> In this very moment all that translates to: Mage Pirates, Changeling Pirates is fine and even Demon Pirates is fine. Curious about what all these gamelines might give us, since I agree with some more than others. But Pirate Geist is also thing that must happen.<br /> <br /> EDIT: If I may add something, I can totally see Demon being related to nautical history, but I won't make it Pirate. Some of the weirdest and most famous supernatural stories and tropes related to the sea would work great within a Demon framework, it's just that most of those are not related to the Age of Piracy. Again, if this happens, then I'll be optimist about it, but I think there's more potential elsewhere","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 07-07-2017, 08:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T06:15:32-07:00","id":1112629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1112601#post1112601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Pirate Geist is also thing that must happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. It not only fits, but if any line is book-starved, it is Geist (even over Mummy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T06:25:32-07:00","id":1112636,"title":"","content":"I'm kinda sold on Western Promethean/Werewolf now, even if railroad Infrastructure is evocative. Ulgans are a natural overlap between the two splats, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T06:51:51-07:00","id":1112647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1112636#post1112636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kinda sold on Western Promethean/Werewolf now, even if railroad Infrastructure is evocative. Ulgans are a natural overlap between the two splats, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the overlap between Promethean/Geist is also interesting - New Beginnings and Second Chances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T06:56:27-07:00","id":1112649,"title":"","content":"We are at 646 voted on Pirate Era and Mage, Changeling and Geist having exactly 22% of votes, with Mage having few votes more. We must be ready for Pirate Changeling...<br /> <br /> That can be even good thing... <br /> <br /> If we still get Mage on Pirates to get whole Nameless cult from Pirate Republic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T07:00:55-07:00","id":1112650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1112649#post1112649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are at 646 voted on Pirate Era and Mage, Changeling and Geist having exactly 22% of votes, with Mage having few votes more. We must be ready for Pirate Changeling...<br /> <br /> That can be even good thing...<br /> <br /> If we still get Mage on Pirates to get whole Nameless cult from Pirate Republic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything can happen. We need to hit $55000 first, which looks like it may take a while at this rate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T07:05:35-07:00","id":1112652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1112649#post1112649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are at 646 voted on Pirate Era and Mage, Changeling and Geist having exactly 22% of votes, with Mage having few votes more. We must be ready for Pirate Changeling...</div> </div> </div> </div>I swear, I love all the gamelines and one of my favorites is Werewolf, not a minor one by a long stretch, but being a special fan of the &quot;less-loved ones&quot;, if you pass me the term at least when it comes to sheer popularity, is not always easy.<br /> <br /> A feeling I'm sure other people share. Jeez, I promise I'll stop being a big grumpy baby, just give me a minute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T07:08:46-07:00","id":1112653,"title":"","content":"if we won't get Geist Age of Piracy, I will be furious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T07:19:51-07:00","id":1112662,"title":"","content":"On a related note, I don't know it was intentional, but knowing Onyx Path are a bunch of smart people I'd say that having the starting Eras of the book being all made of popular/big gamelines sharing the chapter with less popular/new gamelines was both a cunning idea, a way to give everyone a chance to shine and an excellent promotional move. The authors do get all my praise for that.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps I'm imagining things and it's all a coincidence. I've been wrong before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T07:49:07-07:00","id":1112674,"title":"","content":"I voted Changeling for the pirate era, because... well. Press-gangs and Shanghaiing fit the theme of Changeling perfectly, and there is so much exciting maritime lore, with things like Fiddler's Green, and all kinds of exciting sea monsters, such as mermaids.<br /> <br /> Edit: And my favourite game line is Werewolf. So it's not just that I'm a Changeling fan. If it wasn't for the Silver Ladder/Seers Team Up, I'd have said that Golden Age of Piracy should've been Changeling/Geist. But I NEED to hear that Seer/Silver Ladder story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T07:57:02-07:00","id":1112678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1112674#post1112674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I voted Changeling for the pirate era, because... well. Press-gangs and Shanghaiing fit the theme of Changeling perfectly, and there is so much exciting maritime lore, with things like Fiddler's Green, and all kinds of exciting sea monsters, such as mermaids.<br /> <br /> Edit: And my favourite game line is Werewolf. So it's not just that I'm a Changeling fan. If it wasn't for the Silver Ladder/Seers Team Up, I'd have said that Golden Age of Piracy should've been Changeling/Geist. But I NEED to hear that Seer/Silver Ladder story.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all cool, I really don't want to make this an aggressive feud of sort. I'm just having a little fun and trying to vent grumpiness with a little bit of self-mockery.<br /> <br /> In all seriousness, jokes and fake vicious rivalries aside, whatever people vote and whatever wins, it's all absolutely fine. Everyone has the right to do as they want, no need to justify any choice. We're still gonna get great material in the end and if Changeling wins, it was among my top three choices for the Era anyways<br /> <br /> <b><i>Pirate Geist though</i></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 07-07-2017, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T08:06:43-07:00","id":1112684,"title":"","content":"I wonder if winning game lines from previous polls should be excluded from future ones in order to have more balanced representations. I worry about Mage and Changeling crushing all opposition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T08:09:46-07:00","id":1112685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1112684#post1112684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if winning game lines from previous polls should be excluded from future ones in order to have more balanced representations. I worry about Mage and Changeling crushing all opposition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would expect so","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T08:22:53-07:00","id":1112689,"title":"","content":"well, it was mentioned that sometimes it would be people voting for an Era a certain gameline would get, and I assume that they may give a more narrow choice of gamelines if they'll see that all of them end up as the same gameline. I assume we should just wait and watch how things go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T08:28:22-07:00","id":1112692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1112684#post1112684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if winning game lines from previous polls should be excluded from future ones in order to have more balanced representations. I worry about Mage and Changeling crushing all opposition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not every poll will be 'Here's an era, what two splats do you want?' They mentioned this beforehand in the e-mail, I think. Plus the 'put your gameline in an era' people are a wildcard and currently there's five of them, then there's two 'failed era' and one 'your own era' people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T08:37:45-07:00","id":1112699,"title":"","content":"I was all for a Beast/Geist, Flying Dutch and Kraken and all that. So I voted Beast, expecting Geist to be overwhelming. Seeing the rise of Mages and Changelings, I changed my vote to Geist, because there's no way we won't have Geist Pirates !!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T08:42:36-07:00","id":1112704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nepher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1112699#post1112699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">because there's no way we won't have Geist Pirates !!!</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do people want pirates who go around putting ghosts to rest?<br /> <br /> Is it like wydhamster points out, just because of the Pirates of the Caribbean movies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T08:42:42-07:00","id":1112705,"title":"","content":"So, I chatted with Matthew about crowdsourcing some suggestions for research resources. He thought it was a good idea, so I've made a thread <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1112393-reference-and-research-for-dark-eras-2\">here</a>. If you know of any good non-fiction resources for any of the eras in DE2, I know the dev team would appreciate if you make a note of them in that thread so they know to take a look at them. I've got something for most of the eras, but I don't have any sources for Qing China or Golden Age of Piracy off the top of my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 05-31-2019, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T09:08:57-07:00","id":1112720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1112704#post1112704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why do people want pirates who go around putting ghosts to rest?<br /> <br /> Is it like wydhamster points out, just because of the Pirates of the Caribbean movies?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't speak for everyone- but for me, it is ghost ships, restless souls which are forced to roam the seas, the mixture of traditions and superstitions from all around the globe, the search for hidden treasures known only for dead people and, of course, the connection between the ocean and the Underworld, as presented in CofD (the rivers of the dead and the Ocean of Fragments).<br /> <br /> Yeah, the Pirates of the Caribbean are, without doubt, an helpful image for what Pirate Geist may look like- but Pirates of the Caribbean didn't invented the concept of ghost ship. The trope is much wider and richer than that. The same thing could also be said about Geist- there is more about it than going around and putting souls to rest. It is also about investigating the Underworld, making up your own history and mythology and celebrating life while being dead. It is about roaming in lands which have never seen by any living man before, going lost in labyrinths of fog and despair, rising a toast for dead people and finding treasures lost from before time. It is about both freedom and commitment, following your own code of honor while bound by strange laws no one truly understand.<br /> <br /> I don't know about you- but that sounds like a pirate's life for me :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T09:12:34-07:00","id":1112723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1112704#post1112704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why do people want pirates who go around putting ghosts to rest?<br /> <br /> Is it like wydhamster points out, just because of the Pirates of the Caribbean movies?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pirates of the Caribbean is the last of a long tradition. Remember: it's the adaptation of a theme park attraction, not something especially original. Ghost ships, skeleton crews, famous pirates returning from the deads, highly supersticious sailors... This was a thing then, and it imbued pirate fiction since the beginning. So much that there were already Ghost Pirates in the original Scooby Doo !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T09:26:33-07:00","id":1112732,"title":"","content":"Yeah pretty excited for the 1001 Nights Era. The Islamic Golden Age is fascinating history!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T09:34:31-07:00","id":1112736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1112704#post1112704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why do people want pirates who go around putting ghosts to rest?<br /> <br /> Is it like wydhamster points out, just because of the Pirates of the Caribbean movies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghosts and ships are things that go together very frequently, Pirates of The Caribbean movies aside.<br /> <br /> One could argue that elements of Changeling and Werewolf are also a thing with nautical folklore, and I agree, don't get me wrong. Mysterious disappearances, monsters and weird worlds, they're all there but, on a wider perspective, the most recurrent stories are the one about ghosts.<br /> <br /> Partially, it's because of the literary influences that forged our modern pop culture, from which I I personally would choose William Hope Hodgson as the master of the &quot;supernatural ocean&quot; genre. But even him tapped into the vast horizon of nautical folklore about ghosts and monsters. The Age of Piracy pretty much is the first era that comes to mind when one thinks about sea and monsters and the most recurrent topos of myths is that of the ghost. Ghost ships were not invented by Pirates or by Monkey Island, though we can agree it's to them they might owe their current popularity.<br /> <br /> The thing is, during the history of sailing, the one recurrent element among all crews was the bizarre form of syncretism between the faith of each sailor combined with that of its brothers and shaped by the experience of sailing itself. That's a really Geist thing, were you have legends about Catholic Saints and &quot;pagan&quot; spirits guarding over you, of Satan playing cards with men to steal their soul and of Underworlds, superstitions, rules and death rituals that don't align with the dogmas and beliefs of those who never left the mainland.<br /> <br /> Without getting too much in the details, seamen always respected and dreaded the ocean as something that could take away their life with ease, giving birth to a lot of stories about death and ghosts. Sure, the monsters were there but, speaking in real world terms, death was a thing that always loomed over everyone. The fear of your soul not being able to move onward, always doomed to sail the sea even in death was, and in some places still is, a very real one. My grandpa was a fishermen from Southern Italy born in the 20th century, but he still knew many little weird stories about sailors and death.<br /> <br /> The reason it all leads to people wanting a Pirate Era about Geist it's because no other era embodies legends about the sea, the ships and the sailors as much as that one. It is a truly vivid Era that does have solid connections with ghosts and Geist itself, with elements about celebrating life and freedom. I can see pretty much any combination happening, but Geist has to be part of it, if you ask me.<br /> <br /> Plus general awesomeness about buried treasures, vengeful pirate ghosts and ships that travel into the Underworld. but that's a given.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ninja'ed by several people. Also totally on board with the excitement for the Islamic Golden Era","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 07-07-2017, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T09:41:29-07:00","id":1112741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1112704#post1112704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why do people want pirates who go around putting ghosts to rest?<br /> <br /> Is it like wydhamster points out, just because of the Pirates of the Caribbean movies?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Even though I'm voting Mage right now, its a strategic vote. Geist is my top pick for this era, and that is despite the fact that I'm pretty much over Pirates of the Caribbean as a franchise that I once loved but has become overly bloated. Pirate Geists hits pretty much ever thematic note you could hope for, and that would be true regardless of Disney's movies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T10:01:50-07:00","id":1112759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1112678#post1112678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's all cool, I really don't want to make this an aggressive feud of sort. I'm just having a little fun and trying to vent grumpiness with a little bit of self-mockery.<br /> <br /> In all seriousness, jokes and fake vicious rivalries aside, whatever people vote and whatever wins, it's all absolutely fine. Everyone has the right to do as they want, no need to justify any choice. We're still gonna get great material in the end and if Changeling wins, it was among my top three choices for the Era anyways<br /> <br /> <b><i>Pirate Geist though</i></b></div> </div> </div> </div> Changeling is my favourite line, but thematically Geist fits Pirate to a T. <br /> <br /> Ghosts, Pirates , and Rum, the Geist Era would practically write itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T10:02:00-07:00","id":1112760,"title":"","content":"...meanwhile I seem to be the only guy that remembers that PotC was a theme park attraction first over a movie franchise...<br /> <br /> ...damn kids and your iPhones and your social media...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T10:02:59-07:00","id":1112762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1112741#post1112741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Even though I'm voting Mage right now, its a strategic vote. Geist is my top pick for this era, and that is despite the fact that I'm pretty much over Pirates of the Caribbean as a franchise that I once loved but has become overly bloated. Pirate Geists hits pretty much ever thematic note you could hope for, and that would be true regardless of Disney's movies.</div> </div> </div> </div> Agreed 100% I voted Geist personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T10:14:42-07:00","id":1112769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1112684#post1112684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if winning game lines from previous polls should be excluded from future ones in order to have more balanced representations. I worry about Mage and Changeling crushing all opposition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mage won only a single vote in Dark Eras 1's kickstarter, and that was the one everyone was cheating on before we fixed the voting software. (to be fair, everyone was cheating in favour of the other games, too). It got the exisitng era expanded by a Special Backer, and half of another setting added by a second Special Backer.<br /> <br /> It's just that the Golden Age of Piracy is explicitly mentioned in Awakening 2e's corebook as a historical curiosity of note - it's the last major alliance between the Diamond and the Seers, versus mages who would be Free Councillors in the modern day, around the failed pirate state of Nassau.<br /> <br /> Or, another way, Neall played too much Assassins Creed Black Flag.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custo