ty of outsiders that has to regulate itself and is at war with a arguably superior power&quot; that works well with pirates","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T13:43:30-07:00","id":1115230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1115224#post1115224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PotC Davy Jones', being a psychopomp that makes pact that alter those involved and has access to planes of existence and items normal people don't, honestly can be represented by a quite big variety of CoD splats.</div> </div> </div> </div> No kidding. Mummy and Vamprie are probably the biggest stretches, but even those can have workable concepts. <br /> <br /> Seriously... An eldritch, unkillable creature with some perifieral connections to the Lovecraft Mythos who has minons steeped in occult lore in various states of not being human anymore hiding away a precious magical item of personal importance in a &quot;Dead Man's Chest&quot; as a result of dealings with a ancient, capricious, and dangerous deity? Can you get a character who is any more like one of the Arisen in a mainstream movie without falling back on the trappings of Ancient Egypt?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1115224#post1115224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I persoanly think Changeling is contender because of its sheer popularity, because of merfolk and sirens and of mysterious disappearances at sea. Plus the whole &quot;society of outsiders that has to regulate itself and is at war with a arguably superior power&quot; that works well with pirates</div> </div> </div> </div>In general, I'm personally disenclined to credit PotC with the popularity of this era for exactly this reason. Pirates have always been hugely popular and have on the greatest corpuses of folklore surrounding them in the world, which this demonstrates in spades. That mythology is broadly applicable across every game that CofD has produced. No blockbusters needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https:/