s having rather bloated (???) crossover section - and surely limited exploration of Mage setting from it's perspective. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire\">Just see my comments on limited treatment of Diamond mages it when it got in my hands</a>, half year ago...<br /> <br /> I hope that limited word count in Dark Eras 2 would not squash some important themes on gamelines presented like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you kidding? Princes of the Conquered Land was pretty much <i>the pitch perfect</i> example of a crossover setting. The second best thing we have is Sundered World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T21:40:12-07:00","id":1115786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1115784#post1115784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there anyway to see the current poll results? I keep getting sent to the voting options, and I want to see current results</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you vote originally on a mobile device or a computer? If my guess about what they did to the poll is right (and it may not be) you may only be able to see the results if you voted with a laptop or desktop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T21:43:27-07:00","id":1115788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1115778#post1115778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a possibility that your feelings are coloured by the fact that you don't like Mummy Wyrd? Cause I think that Mutapa was goddamn awesome, and was a breath of fresh air for Mage. Personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe - but this also example that in crossover Era, somethings cructial to one Era maybe omitted by word count. <i>Like whole deal with not mentioning Diamond conversion of local Shaona or Muslim Diamond in area in Era about this cultures meeting. </i><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As we are about it - I still look for Islamic Gold Age as Changeling with proposed Vampire and Beast - <b>but I <i>really </i>would like to hear at least a bit about original Islamic Diamond mages</b> - to finally mark them on the time-space of region, maybe with pointing that they may come from Carthage. Fingers crossed for having them in Beasts crossovers one page additions! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On the other hand, seeing how <i>Princes of Conquered Lands</i> have not expended for material above in crossover - I'm worried we will not see anything beyond one sentence in 'Chronicles of Darkness' sidebar on other gamelines matters, contrary to <i>Fearful Lesson</i> Beast Era... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-14-2017, 12:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T21:47:44-07:00","id":1115790,"title":"","content":"Mind you I haven't pledged to this kickstarter, so my input is limited-but I would be bored as fucking hell if they went with the obvious choice of Changeling with 1001 Nights. The current pairing is inventive and fine-even a better fit than Changeling, actually.<br /> <br /> Also, Hamster, you keep making this assumption that culture is particularly a thing for the Diamond. It's not. That's the entire fucking point of To The Strongest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T21:55:46-07:00","id":1115791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1115790#post1115790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you I haven't pledged to this kickstarter, so my input is limited-but I would be bored as fucking hell if they went with the obvious choice of Changeling with 1001 Nights. The current pairing is inventive and fine-even a better fit than Changeling, actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. I was on board with Golden Age Changeling, especially because I like Changeling as Jinn, but now that the initial surprise at Vampire/Beast has worn off and sunk in, I like this much better. Not the least because it is a surprising combination that still makes sense for the Era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T22:21:26-07:00","id":1115802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1115785#post1115785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you kidding? Princes of the Conquered Land was pretty much <i>the pitch perfect</i> example of a crossover setting. The second best thing we have is Sundered World.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not so sure it's perfect crossover - in Mage part of Era, at least, there are no story hooks or timeline materia\u0142 about Mummy. It does not sound as 'full crossover'..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T22:31:42-07:00","id":1115806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1115790#post1115790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Hamster, you keep making this assumption that culture is particularly a thing for the Diamond. It's not. That's the entire fucking point of To The Strongest.</div> </div> </div> </div>2E Mage makes actually diffrent point - Orders comes from particular time and place, not just some fairytale land. There are thousands of mages outside of Diamond - and many would be ofended implying that their culture is not important. Hell, it's clue of 2E Free Council AND Princes of Conquered Land Dark Era! <br /> If I'm wrong, show me in Era text. Because right now Diamond till 300 BCE was non existing, was somewhere created before 200 BCE and somehow he would need to show up in Islamic Empire. <br /> <br /> Also, Islamic Golden Age is precisly at time when Tremere Order join Diamond Orders from Eastern Europe - very much, please mark it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T22:47:08-07:00","id":1115812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1115806#post1115806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2E Mage makes actually diffrent point - Orders comes from particular time and place, not just some fairytale land. There are thousands of mages outside of Diamond - and many would be ofended implying that their culture is not important. Hell, it's clue of 2E Free Council AND Princes of Conquered Land Dark Era!<br /> If I'm wrong, show me in Era text. Because right now Diamond till 300 BCE was non existing, was somewhere created before 200 BCE and somehow he would need to show up in Islamic Empire.<br /> <br /> Also, Islamic Golden Age is precisly at time when Tremere Order join Diamond Orders from Eastern Europe - very much, please mark it!</div> </div> </div> </div>Hamster, the thread you linked to has tons of people who not only make a contradictory point to what you posit-including the developer-but also articulates the nuance of the Diamond in relation to various cultures way better than you do.<br /> <br /> Being blunt, at what point do you expect me disregard the mass of of informed opinion over one person's interpretation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T23:05:36-07:00","id":1115816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1115812#post1115812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hamster, the thread you linked to has tons of people who not only make a contradictory point to what you posit-including the developer-but also articulates the nuance of the Diamond in relation to various cultures way better than you do.<br /> <br /> Being blunt, at what point do you expect me disregard the mass of of informed opinion over one person's interpretation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Diamonds Orders world hegemony did not become reality in one night - it was not like Great Refusal - and even this Free Council creation took <i>century </i>to finlize. Just point me from where Diamond came to Islamic World and something about local Nameless Orders and/or Darshanas. That's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T23:18:31-07:00","id":1115819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1115816#post1115816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Diamonds Orders world hegemony did not become reality in one night - it was not like Great Refusal - and even this Free Council creation took <i>century </i>to finlize. Just point me from where Diamond came to Islamic World and something about local Nameless Orders and/or Darshanas. That's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hamster, it took over 800 years before Islam was even <i>a thing</i>. I think the recourse was pretty well a thing by then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T00:34:44-07:00","id":1115832,"title":"","content":"Funnily enough for me the new poll was an opportunity to change my vote. I initially voted for Beast (because I love Beasts, and also krakens are cool) but as I think it's the most deserving of the setting I voted for Geist this time.<br /> <br /> Now if we can get Geist Second edition with it, that'd be cool <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T00:53:43-07:00","id":1115835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1115802#post1115802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not so sure it's perfect crossover - in Mage part of Era, at least, there are no story hooks or timeline materia\u0142 about Mummy. It does not sound as 'full crossover'..</div> </div> </div> </div>...what?<br /> <br /> There are story seeds. In the back of the chapter. Just like every other Era. It incorporates all the historical elements that come from the Mutapa Empire that the chapter had previously mentioned, and it includes various bits and pieces on how and why Mages or Mummies would be interested in being involved in said plot seeds.<br /> <br /> I'm starting to think you didn't actually read much of the chapter and only cherry-picked whatever was convenient for your argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T03:01:04-07:00","id":1115857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1115816#post1115816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Diamonds Orders world hegemony did not become reality in one night - it was not like Great Refusal - and even this Free Council creation took <i>century </i>to finlize. Just point me from where Diamond came to Islamic World and something about local Nameless Orders and/or Darshanas. That's it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The area the Abbasid Caliphate would rise in had earlier been Alexandrian Empire where the Diamond Orders were born. They were well established there long before Islam.<br /> <br /> There are regions of the world that I do think the Diamond Orders came too much later. It's easy to see Norse Mages in the Viking Era not having assimiliated into the Diamond Orders that had used the Roman Empire and then the Church to spread elsewhere in Europe; for example. But 750 ce Baghdad is already going to have been firmly Diamond assimilated for almost a millennium.<br /> <br /> Not that there wouldn't also be Nameless Orders as there always are, but the region is well past the era of Great Cults and Darshanas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T04:06:10-07:00","id":1115867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1115790#post1115790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you I haven't pledged to this kickstarter, so my input is limited-but I would be bored as fucking hell if they went with the obvious choice of Changeling with 1001 Nights. The current pairing is inventive and fine-even a better fit than Changeling, actually.<br /> <br /> Also, Hamster, you keep making this assumption that culture is particularly a thing for the Diamond. It's not. That's the entire fucking point of To The Strongest.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't care if Changeling is the obvious choice for 1,001 nights, it will help flush out and enhance the Toronto Court and expand on it's history, so I 100% support expanding 1,001 nights to include Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T05:58:08-07:00","id":1115903,"title":"","content":"Islamic Golden Age being Vampire/Beast means that my Djinn Homebrew, which is among the best stuff I ever churned out, still has a reason to be. Good news.<br /> <br /> Speaking more seriously, if a Changeling expansion happens I'll be totally cool with it, but I actually embraced the idea of Vampire and Beast for the Era. Creatures that haunt the nights of Baghdad and 2E Ghilan are interesting, not to mention Islamic Covenants are something that the gameline could really use. As for Beast, well, its a gameline I love for a Era I love, but there are plenty of elements that can be used as resources for it. Lairs, stories &amp; dreams, passion &amp; hungers and all those wonderful monsters you can find in A Thousand And One Nights, just to mention a few.<br /> <br /> As others have said, I respect the developers for being a little daring with the Era,going for unexpected gamelines. Really curious about it, whether it's about being a shapeshifter that lives in the desert and thirst for the blood of the living, a monster living in the court of the Caliph, a predator that stalks the dark corners of the bazar or freaking Roc bird in human shape.<br /> <br /> (Yeah, all those years running a game set in this Era do show. Forgive me about it, but I just can't hold the enthusiasm)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 07-14-2017, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T07:08:08-07:00","id":1115932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1115806#post1115806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2E Mage makes actually diffrent point - Orders comes from particular time and place, not just some fairytale land. There are thousands of mages outside of Diamond - and many would be ofended implying that their culture is not important. Hell, it's clue of 2E Free Council AND Princes of Conquered Land Dark Era! <br /> If I'm wrong, show me in Era text. Because right now Diamond till 300 BCE was non existing, was somewhere created before 200 BCE and somehow he would need to show up in Islamic Empire.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very confusing. Firstly, if I understand you correctly, other cultures ARE offended by Diamond mages showing up trying to 'educate' local shaman - that's the whole Era's basis of conflict.<br /> <br /> Secondly, what is this bit about 200 bce? Is it a typo? Something from Mage history I'm unaware of? Or do you not know when Islam began?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T07:12:43-07:00","id":1115936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1115932#post1115932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is very confusing. Firstly, if I understand you correctly, other cultures ARE offended by Diamond mages showing up trying to 'educate' local shaman - that's the whole Era's basis of conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it is - not all Nameless joined Diamond. That's why we have Free Council at the dawn of XX century.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1115932#post1115932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly, what is this bit about 200 bce? Is it a typo? Something from Mage history I'm unaware of? Or do you not know when Islam began?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2E Mage corebook there is pointed that Adamantine Arrow as Order started before 200 BCE. So it's more or less closest date to start of other Diamond Orders as organizations.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T08:39:18-07:00","id":1115954,"title":"","content":"I'm honestly curious what the mood/theme of 1,001 Nights is supposed to be, myself. The Era actually covers two massively different time periods which have extremely different feelings to them. The fairy tale feeling of 1,001 Nights, with genies and magical caves and fisherman tales and raunchy sexuality (and the quiet moral edge underneath it all), doesn't fit vampiric predation, though you can maybe put Beasts in there as the creators of cautionary tales.<br /> <br /> The Islamic Golden Age, meanwhile, is outlined as a time of grandeur and wonderment thanks to its leaps forward in social institutions and technological progress. It's a pretty big thematic and atmospheric change to the whole &quot;Wonders of the unknown laying beyond the city&quot; thing when the city itself is a seat of progress and attainment.<br /> <br /> The Era would probably be best served by ending it around 630 CE and making the Golden Age its own Era if people really wanted to explore it. Drop Vampire, put in Changeling, because while a Vampire can serve one fairy tale story, they can't serve them all. Changelings can.<br /> <br /> That's my two cents. I'd honestly really like it if the blurbs for the Eras included what thematic elements in a given Era were being honed in on and why. I'd also like it if future votes on eras were for preset settings, rather than &quot;Pick which you feel fit the Era best&quot;, because some things really do work better together than others. Much as I love Mage, the Great War Era really does belong best to Geist and Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T09:24:03-07:00","id":1115979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1115867#post1115867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't care if Changeling is the obvious choice for 1,001 nights, it will help flush out and enhance the Toronto Court and expand on it's history, so I 100% support expanding 1,001 nights to include Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Toronto's Scheherazade Court is it's own thing though? The history of changelings in the Islamic Golden Age isn't going to reflect much on the history and mechanics of Toronto in anything more than the sort of stuff you'd get from this era regardless of what gameline is tied to it. Hell, the original freehold that was imported into Toronto before it was adjusted is itself divorced from the era in all <i>but</i> the story, because the changelings who brought it over lived in a different context from the era.<br /> <br /> More on point, if you're reducing the Islamic Golden Age to 1,001 Nights, you are missing the brilliance of the era. Beasts let us walk somewhat in the popular subject, sure, but Vampires and Beasts rips our eyes away from that subject and let us really look at the rest of the time period-which is good, because the Islamic Golden Age is chock full of awesome.<br /> <br /> It would be a waste if the era was more about Scheherazade than, say, Nasir al-Din al-Tusi.<br /> <br /> PS: Also we have no idea how Toronto is going to look in 2nd Edition, so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T09:56:24-07:00","id":1115997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1115979#post1115979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Toronto's Scheherazade Court is it's own thing though? The history of changelings in the Islamic Golden Age isn't going to reflect much on the history and mechanics of Toronto in anything more than the sort of stuff you'd get from this era regardless of what gameline is tied to it. Hell, the original freehold that was imported into Toronto before it was adjusted is itself divorced from the era in all <i>but</i> the story, because the changelings who brought it over lived in a different context from the era.<br /> <br /> More on point, if you're reducing the Islamic Golden Age to 1,001 Nights, you are missing the brilliance of the era. Beasts let us walk somewhat in the popular subject, sure, but Vampires and Beasts rips our eyes away from that subject and let us really look at the rest of the time period-which is good, because the Islamic Golden Age is chock full of awesome.<br /> <br /> It would be a waste if the era was more about Scheherazade than, say, Nasir al-Din al-Tusi.<br /> <br /> PS: Also we have no idea how Toronto is going to look in 2nd Edition, so.</div> </div> </div> </div> I didn't suggest you couldn't explore the wider situation during the Islamic Golden Age, they likely will, and I do understand that alot has changed since that time, BUT it goes right to the present, so exploring the origins of the Court back in the Islamic Golden Age, including any effect of the political cultural upon it, then flashing forward to the current present state and how its evovled and moved ahead could be interesting.<br /> <br /> Plus Iran would be a place were the True Fae run free , since the fall of the Shah, peehaps throughout most of the middle east, and that could be explored as well, perhaps it has its roots way back during the Islamic Golden Era which eventually lead later on to the rise in influence and power of the True Fae in the region.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 07-14-2017, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T10:02:55-07:00","id":1116001,"title":"","content":"Hey, sudden question: When exactly <i>is</i> the One Thousand and One Nights Era set? I just went back to look and confirm something and ended up spotting an error: The banner for it says 750 B.C.E. (which would include a Pre-Islamic Era) and the text beneath says 750 C.E. (which is the time period commonly agreed upon for the Golden Age).<br /> <br /> Gonna tag <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2\" data-vbnamecard=\"2\">Rose Bailey</a> so this can be corrected, if it hasn't been brought up already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T10:04:37-07:00","id":1116003