://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T23:00:22-07:00","id":1118409,"title":"","content":"This one seems to be going a lot slower than usual, for a variety of reasons I suppose. I do believe it's going to hit that first stretch goal, apparently backers popping in near the end is common.<br /> <br /> But, in the case that it didn't, I wonder what the 'Creator of Darkness' backers would do. They're able to put in an era that didn't get put in. And there's two of them. Would they get a list of potential stretch goals? Even if Piracy is in, with five 'Expander of Darkness' backers it looks like most eras will have three gamelines, or at least some will have four.<br /> <br /> It's an interesting one. Sad to see the enthusiasm from the first one gone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T23:22:54-07:00","id":1118417,"title":"","content":"Yeah I'm wondering what's going on.<br /> <br /> Like, is right now just a bad time for gamers financially and people are hesitant to put in money they can't afford to spend frivolously right now? Were people just that disappointed in what DE1 and DEC ended up being?<br /> <br /> Or...are people making good on their promise on boycotting nuWW...by also boycotting OPP? Even though there are a lot of explanations and testimonies out there on why doing so just harms OPP more even though they did nothing wrong? Or due to certain freelancers leaving OPP under not-so-amicable circumstances and people refusing to back as an act of solidarity with said freelancers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T00:00:20-07:00","id":1118421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1118417#post1118417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Were people just that disappointed in what DE1 and DEC ended up being?</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't heard anything like that, save for some frustration about the Changeling material not necessarily completely working with where 2E is going to end up. Overall Dark Eras was very well received<br /> <br /> I think the biggest issue was it's too soon. People got the Companion only a few months ago. There isn't a lot of hunger for more of the same stuff immediately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T00:02:11-07:00","id":1118422,"title":"","content":"What I'd suggest if there aren't a lot of options for resurrection-backers to resurrect, is that they get to pitch Eras, and the people who paid to pitch eras get extra word count for those chapters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T00:09:34-07:00","id":1118423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1118417#post1118417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I'm wondering what's going on.<br /> <br /> Like, is right now just a bad time for gamers financially and people are hesitant to put in money they can't afford to spend frivolously right now? Were people just that disappointed in what DE1 and DEC ended up being?<br /> <br /> Or...are people making good on their promise on boycotting nuWW...by also boycotting OPP? Even though there are a lot of explanations and testimonies out there on why doing so just harms OPP more even though they did nothing wrong? Or due to certain freelancers leaving OPP under not-so-amicable circumstances and people refusing to back as an act of solidarity with said freelancers?</div> </div> </div> </div>You've got my reason for not backing in there.<br /> <br /> Everyone also seems to be forgetting that DE1 previewed the full text of the book to everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T00:22:21-07:00","id":1118427,"title":"","content":"There's probably a wide number of factors contributing to it being slow. Whether or not that means anything now is not particularly relevant, though. What'll be alarming is if the final push is muted, and if so, by how much.<br /> <br /> I'll admit, I'd be surprised if it actually was strongly related to company image issues, regardless of how you go about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T01:25:59-07:00","id":1118440,"title":"","content":"well, I must admit that I am yet to back the Kickstarter, for a number of reasons- the first is personal financial problems, which means I am now on a &quot;save money&quot; state. That goes with the fact the minimal amount of money needed to back the project and still get, well, something is much higher- 20$ instead of 1$ (sure, at the old 1$ pledge I would have got only Eras which belong to the gameline I choose to back and at 20$ I get the whole book, but it is still kinda discouraging). The fact that you back the whole book automatically instead of individual lines removes a little bit of the &quot;competitive&quot; factor, which harms the excitement a little. The second, and the more important reason, is that I just can't feel &quot;excited&quot; about this Kickstarter. I try, I really do, but I feel like something is missing. The lack of a preview seems to be an important factor, as the small paragraphs about each Era are nice, but still not enough to catch my interest. I don't know what the plans are for each of the Eras, or what special and weird things make those Eras special other than &quot;Chinese mummies&quot; or &quot;vampires in the french revolution&quot;. Also, for some reason, I dislike having crossover eras as the &quot;core concept&quot; of the book. I prefer individual Eras, each being based around a certain gameline, with an option to increase to Crossover through stretch goals or pledges, than less Eras with each including two splats. To me, it makes me feel like the Eras are just less &quot;special&quot;. And more than all, I feel like this Kickstarter has just came way too early- I mean, it feels like Dark Eras 1 was just a while ago! There weren't even some teasing about it by writers/developers like it was last time. It all makes it feel a bit blend, to my taste.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm not saying I won't end up backing this project- only that for the time being, I don't feel any need to do so. I hope that something would happen and catch my attention, so I'll want to back the Kickstarter- but for now, I just feel, well, bored, and I can't back Kickstarters which can't catch my interest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T01:41:24-07:00","id":1118444,"title":"","content":"To be fair, going be DE 2, the crossover chapters will have plenty without having to use crossovers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T01:43:54-07:00","id":1118445,"title":"","content":"I said it before and others agree, but yeah, not having a full preview is likely a big factor.<br /> <br /> I also never expected for Dark Eras 2 to happen so soon after we got the Companion (in theory, I realize writing it and all will require lots of time) and while that has not compromised my enthusiams, I admit I thought it would come after Deviant's Kickstarter and Changeling release, at least. It kinda popped out of nowhere with little &quot;advertising&quot; or preparation, if you get what I' trying to say. Not an issue for me, but I understand that's a valid point to bring up","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 07-20-2017, 04:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T02:13:14-07:00","id":1118455,"title":"","content":"I think one thing likely hurting it is that for many people, more historical settings aren't what they want right now. The folks who are counting down the days until Changeling, Hunter, Geist, and Mummy get updated to the new edition aren't exactly drooling over supplemenal content when they still don't have corebooks yet, and a historical setting is very niche compared to a broader suppement book: I think more Werewolf and Mage fans are hungry for standalone books than settings they will almost certainly never run. I say all of this as a diehard history nerd who wishes we were drowning in more of them; this is a niche product, coming out at a time when other things feel much more pressing for much of the fanbase, and without some of the crucial benefits its predecessor had going for it, to say nothing of ongoing boycotts and the like. Dark Eras is a product that needs a strong base to build from, and right now it really does not have that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T02:19:28-07:00","id":1118459,"title":"","content":"I haven't backed it. Yet.<br /> I will have by tomorrow, when I get money.<br /> I was simply reeling from the Steam Summer Sale. If I had known this was coming so soon, I would have set money aside for it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T05:24:38-07:00","id":1118489,"title":"","content":"I know for myself, my lack of enthusiasm is down to a couple of reasons.<br /> <br /> The first is that when the first Dark Eras book was on Kickstarter I was just desperate for more Mummy content. Since the Mummy line appeared to be basically finished, new mechanics and concepts were only likely to come through Dark Eras. That made it enormously attractive (also a book full of historical settings is inherently useful when running a game where flashbacks can take you to any time or place on the planet, even if they aren't written specifically for Mummy). I'm not running Mummy anymore though. I still love it to bits, but it also feels a lot more complete than it did pre-Companion and pre-Rio. All the big missing pieces are filled in, save perhaps for a more detailed look at Apotheosis and post-Apotheosis Chronicles. Oh, and this ties more into point three below, but Chinese Mummy isn't interesting to me. It feels like an attempt to win over those people who keep asking for non-Egyptian Mummies in Mummy: The Curse, since China is usually mentioned second only to Inca in those discussions, and that puts me off.<br /> <br /> The second big reason is that I just don't like crossover eras. I'm a purist, I like to focus on one game at a time and explore its themes and complexities while generally leaving crossover to little more than vague hints and Easter Eggs in my games. I am happy that the Mummy crossover is with Hunter, arguably the least intrusive of the other games, but Chinese Mummy doesn't <br /> <br /> Third, there is only one era that really, really grabs me by the lapels and shouts, &quot;I am a perfect fit&quot; the way a lot of the original eras did. And it's for Geist (and not Werewolf, just the Geist half, another issue with the crossover element). And sadly Geist is a game I've by and large decided I will not run unless the second edition is well received, because everything I've ever heard about its mechanics in first edition make them out to be a hot mess.<br /> <br /> I'm not too fussed that Geist, for example, may end up written using first edition text while the second edition is in production. The same happened for Promethean, and I've been using the Dust Bowl as the setting for my Promethean game. There wasn't much in the way of new mechanics, and I wasn't going to use the &quot;canon&quot; content much anyway.<br /> <br /> I want to say I'll back it for the Geist era alone in the hopes Geist one day becomes a game I want to run. But honestly, I may just buy the PDF if that day ever comes instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T07:38:48-07:00","id":1118545,"title":"","content":"Kickstarter fatigue may also be a factor too and I really think that the lack of preview has played a big role. If there is a Dark Eras 3 (Inshallah) I'd hope at least that they develop an outline like we got of Thousand Years of Night, Signs of Sorcery, and The Pack. But as Arc said, there a lot of factors, so it's hard to pin down.<br /> <br /> I'm not worried though. Even if we continue at this slow $200 rate, we'll hit the first stretch goal with five days remaining in the Kickstarter, and anyone can tell you that it's the last 48 hours at the real backing flurry happens, so I think we are looking at 3-4 eras being added outside of the backer additionals. If the backing pace picks up a bit before that last push, we could be looking at more. I'm also hoping that once the stretch goals start coming in, more people will be inclined to back the project. And someone picking up that last $750 Collaberator Tier, as well as some of the $250/$350 pledges would really help catalyze things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T08:18:24-07:00","id":1118565,"title":"","content":"Personally I backed it, but that's because I didn't back the first one (to my regret) and am using this as an opportunity to get DE1, DE: Companion, CofD and Hurt Locker all in PDF. DE2 in print is just a bonus really. I could see if I had gotten the first one where this one wouldn't have me fired up the same way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T09:41:03-07:00","id":1118595,"title":"","content":"I'll back it once I have funds available. The lack of a cheaper buy-in option this time held me back thus far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T10:19:57-07:00","id":1118603,"title":"","content":"I mostly backed because I liked DE1. The possibility of Sin-Eater pirates helped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T11:01:43-07:00","id":1118622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1118603#post1118603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mostly backed because I liked DE1. The possibility of Sin-Eater pirates helped.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whereas I backed it for the chance of faerie pirates and mermaids.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T11:06:04-07:00","id":1118627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1118622#post1118622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whereas I backed it for the chance of faerie pirates and mermaids.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not both?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T11:15:32-07:00","id":1118633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1118622#post1118622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whereas I backed it for the chance of faerie pirates and mermaids.</div> </div> </div> </div>If someone gives me a good enough pitch, I may consider (just consider, not guarantee) adding Changeling to Pirates. It would be sweet to get a Mage/Changeling/Geist crossover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T11:46:50-07:00","id":1118642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1118633#post1118633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If someone gives me a good enough pitch, I may consider (just consider, not guarantee) adding Changeling to Pirates. It would be sweet to get a Mage/Changeling/Geist crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think of it. There are so many things that applies.<br /> There are the myths of Fiddler's Green, the perfect place, that one can reach only through long journeys and hard travels. Where the music never stops, and the dancers never tire. Arcadia is the darkest truth to that I've ever seen.<br /> There are the buccaneers; runaway slaves and deserting soldiers deciding to take up a life of piracy and fight those who held them captive. And there are also press gang crews, grabbing anyone they see to force them to labour under terrible circumstances. And, of course, there are privateers.<br /> And the ocean is full of myths! From mermaids, and sea monsters to strange godlike beings who steal away those who disappear into the dark depths.<br /> <br /> Really, the era would be a perfect Changeling/Geist one. If it weren't for the stories about Nassau, I'd never back Mage here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T12:03:14-07:00","id":1118649,"title":"","content":"Unsure if it's been mentioned, but the Islamic Golden Age section on the Kickstarter has been updated to limit the time frame. One Thousand and One Nights - Islamic Golden Age (750 to 1258).'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T12:22:19-07:00","id":1118659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1118649#post1118649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unsure if it's been mentioned, but the Islamic Golden Age section on the Kickstarter has been updated to limit the time frame. One Thousand and One Nights - Islamic Golden Age (750 to 1258).'</div> </div> </div> </div>Finally. Glad to see that, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T12:22:39-07:00","id":1118660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1118649#post1118649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unsure if it's been mentioned, but the Islamic Golden Age section on the Kickstarter has been updated to limit the time frame. One Thousand and One Nights - Islamic Golden Age (750 to 1258).'</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so they are going with the traditional dates then. That gives me something to work with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T14:45:55-07:00","id":1118709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1118627#post1118627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why not both?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I want Mage Pirates. There can only be two...unless someone drops the cash to do an expansion.<br /> <br /> I haven't fully backed yet because few of the Eras I am interested in. Out of all of them, kinda interested in Seven Wonders of the World, because of the upcoming Assassin's Creed game, but not to fond of the gamelines for that era. Interested in the Mage one, because it has Deviants, was a big fan of Mage The Sorcerers Crusade, and one of my fondest memories was reading a AD&amp;D supplement, &quot;A Mighty Fortress&quot;. Really interested in the Islamic Golden Age, huge fan of 1001 Nights. But what will sell me on this back will be if Golden Age of Piracy gets Mage. If it doesn't, I will pass on the kickstarter. Really love that period of history, read many layman books on Caribbean history, but Geist is my least favorite gameline, with Changeling not being high on my list either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2519,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2519-starglyte","user":"Starglyte","date":".  Adding a word 07-20-2017, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2519-starglyte","name":"Starglyte","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T17:50:29-07:00","id":1118772,"title":"","content":"Okay, stop the presses. Fun fact I learned: The Louvre became a museum as a direct result of the French Revolution. The Louvre, one of the greatest collections of art in the world. The Louvre, with one of the most incredible arrays of Egyptian artifacts ever assembles. The Louvre, one of the greatest architectural achievements of France, which would have a litteral glass pyramid placed over it in 1989.<br /> <br /> How is this not a Mummy era?!?<br /> <br /> (On the other hand, I would wholely love to Infrastructure vs Relic Arcitecture be a thing in this era, if not this very building)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T18:14:33-07:00","id":1118777,"title":"","content":"Do people know that Kickstarter doesn't charge you until the project's deadline is met and funded?<br /> <br /> So you can back it now even if you don't have the money but you expect you will in two or three weeks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T18:23:48-07:00","id":1118779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1118772#post1118772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, stop the presses. Fun fact I learned: The Louvre became a museum as a direct result of the French Revolution. The Louvre, one of the greatest collections of art in the world. The Louvre, with one of the most incredible arrays of Egyptian artifacts ever assembles. The Louvre, one of the greatest architectural achievements of France, which would have a litteral glass pyramid placed over it in 1989.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if we're going around then the French Revolution occurred just after the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolf_of_Soissons\" target=\"_blank\">Wolf of Soissons</a> attacks and the infamous attacks of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beast_of_G%C3%A9vaudan\" target=\"_blank\">Beast of G\u00e9vaudan</a>. The area has become the target of the Quicksilver Children, a lodge of scholars introduced in the second edition core who believe that werewolves were created by an idigam. Presumably due to the actions of the Beast, they believe the area is the origin place of werewolves, and seek the idigam there.<br /> <br /> For real fun, in the 1600s of Europe you also have <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thiess_of_Kaltenbrun\" target=\"_blank\">Theiss of Kaltenbrun</a>, a hound of God.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-20-2017, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T19:11:02-07:00","id":1118792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1118777#post1118777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do people know that Kickstarter doesn't charge you until the project's deadline is met and funded?<br /> <br /> So you can back it now even if you don't have the money but you expect you will in two or three weeks.</div> </div> </div> </div>This happens every single time any KS goes up for any company.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T19:23:58-07:00","id":1118800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1118792#post1118792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This happens every single time any KS goes up for any company.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence why the big concern will be if there isn't a huge push at the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T23:27:41-07:00","id":1118850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1118772#post1118772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, stop the presses. Fun fact I learned: The Louvre became a museum as a direct result of the French Revolution. The Louvre, one of the greatest collections of art in the world. The Louvre, with one of the most incredible arrays of Egyptian artifacts ever assembles. The Louvre, one of the greatest architectural achievements of France, which would have a litteral glass pyramid placed over it in 1989.<br /> <br /> How is this not a Mummy era?!?<br /> <br /> (On the other hand, I would wholely love to Infrastructure vs Relic Arcitecture be a thing in this era, if not this very building)</div> </div> </div> </div>Or Mysterium's Atheneum... Which is <i>literal</i> 'mystical museum/library'...<br /> <br /> As we said before - Mage in French Revolution has start of it's <b><i>most fundamental event</i> ( Nameless War ) since creation of Diamond Order in/around Roman Empire</b>. Mummy just have 'we got big collection of Egyptian relics here'...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-21-2017, 02:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T02:18:55-07:00","id":1118871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1118777#post1118777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do people know that Kickstarter doesn't charge you until the project's deadline is met and funded?<br /> <br /> So you can back it now even if you don't have the money but you expect you will in two or three weeks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I try to not write checks I'm not certain will cash. Yes, I could back out, but that throws off metrics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T04:15:02-07:00","id":1118899,"title":"","content":"That's fair.<br /> <br /> I also want to pitch in and say I think the Kickstarter is so slow because, despite the first one being a couple years ago, the delivery of its products was only six months ago. It's just too soon. Possibly people are boycotting because of White Wolf (and they're a little misinformed) and possibly because there's no main text (but I agree with OP's reasons), but mostly it's just so soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T04:59:25-07:00","id":1118909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1118899#post1118899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also want to pitch in and say I think the Kickstarter is so slow because, despite the first one being a couple years ago, the delivery of its products was only six months ago. It's just too soon. Possibly people are boycotting because of White Wolf (and they're a little misinformed) and possibly because there's no main text (but I agree with OP's reasons), but mostly it's just so soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you must also understand that we now crowdfund the book that <i>will be written</i>, not 'is written in 80%', like in Dark Eras 1 was - so be prepared to wait <i>at least </i>one year for PDF of it. ( I myself think it will take more or less 1,5 year from now to get Dark Eras 2 corebook, looking over how Art steps typically took time for OPP freelancers illustrators. )<br /> <br /> From what I understand announcements and updates - single word was not written for the proper Dark Eras 2 for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T05:28:51-07:00","id":1118916,"title":"","content":"The fact that it will take longer until its release doesn't really change the fact that people need to back now when Dark Eras Companion was just released. Besides, the longer wait after backing might be another contributing factor in the lack of backers. I can imagine that people are less willing to back projects that has a longer wait until the product can ship.<br /> <br /> Another contributing factor might be something called &quot;nyhetens behag&quot; in Swedish. I don't know of any similar idiom in English, but it's basically that something that is new and fresh is a lot more attractive than something that has been done before. Even though Dark Eras 2 will contain entire new eras, the concept is identical to Dark Eras 1. Even though I do want Dark Eras 2 I'm certainly not as enthusiastic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T05:45:09-07:00","id":1118925,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the reference and research thread, guys.<br /> <br /> I've been checking one out, was curious about the Chinese era. It suggested Qing meant 'Pure,' though google includes that and a number of other words. They were Manchurians who sort of managed to slip their way in and take over, replacing then <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yangzhou_massacre\" target=\"_blank\">wiping out the Ming</a>. There was apparently some misunderstandings that I'm sure became popular in novels or movies, like a Ming official's wife so sure her husband would remain loyal and die rather than switch sides having her servants and family commit suicide, while the husband just changed sides. They built huge ditches full of willows to keep people out of Manchuria and, legally didn't let non-Manchurians move there. They kept it as a hunting ground for the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imperial_hunt_of_the_Qing_dynasty\" target=\"_blank\">Imperial Hunt</a>. It sounds like the provincial owners wanted the manpower or cheap labor or something to harvest some of the more valuable resources there, like ginseng. I suppose that's a weird inversion of certain modern politics.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> here we just have a general understanding that sequels don't, usually, make as much money or aren't as popular outside of rare instances. I suppose we might call it sequel fatigue but that's usually specific to media.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avata