re</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T18:14:02-07:00","id":1119714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1119712#post1119712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ha!<br /> <br /> No, I was more pointing out that I also really would like to see Arthurian Mage and I have a strong suspicious that a couple of the other four expanders may want it as well given how perfect of a fit they are with one another. Nothing is ever a given, but hope always springs eternal.</div> </div> </div> </div>mage plus werewolf for sir marrock","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T18:49:00-07:00","id":1119727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1119714#post1119714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> mage plus werewolf for sir marrock</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> +Mummy.<br /> <br /> &quot;Go forth and fetch me the Grail Relic, my cultist-knights!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;...Well that could have turned out better.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T18:56:55-07:00","id":1119732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1119568#post1119568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conversely I always found Arthurian stuff to be a bit overdone and gets enough exposure in fictional media, but that's just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd feel that way if the emphasis was on Arthurian <i>Romance</i>, but how much exposure does pre-chivalry sub-Roman Britain get? Mix the history (mostly the Saxons taking other SE England from what I've seen) with some other legends and folkore, maybe the Mabinogion. I'd particularly like that for Werewolf, but I suppose that with <i>Forsaken by Rome, The Wolf and the Raven</i> AND <i>Shadows of the UK</i>, others might be keener on something else.<br /> <br /> And I just remembered how big the Weihan Cynn should be at this point (as any covenants in Britain go). They'll be doing nothing, <i>but</i> cross overs. Whatever splat is featured, you can count on asking a favour from your friendly, blood drinking, possibly golden-eyed neighbour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 07-23-2017, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T21:25:20-07:00","id":1119763,"title":"","content":"Oh man, guys, my five-year hobby in historical sub-Roman Britain (as a result of a three-year hobby in Romantic Arthuriana) is about to become super relevant! Fun fact, I once went to a lecture held by the world expert on Merlin, and had a lovely chat with him afterwards. Seeing Myrddin's Ascension and the shift of the Aeons to include Medruat would be fascinating. If it's Changeling crossover and updates the Lailoken Entitlement that would be equally awesome! Sub-Roman Britain is just such a spectacularly great setting for horror, mostly because of how fatalistic but shiningly optimistic it can be because of how history ended up.<br /> <br /> But then, on the other hand, Epic of Gilgamesh. And Jazz Age. Jazz Age I know less about, but <i>holy crap </i>would Epic of Gilgamesh be awesome. I know they just teased the Utukku with <b>Thousand Years of Night</b>, but seeing a new Extinct Clan would be great, never mind all the other cool stuff from other splats (especially Werwolf).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T21:52:18-07:00","id":1119767,"title":"","content":"And with 165 votes tallied, the three eras are... perfectly deadlocked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a