o it, book-ending it with the Reconstruction Era we already got.<br /> <br /> Also, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maverick_(TV_series\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maverick_(TV_series</a>) and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maverick_(film\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maverick_(film</a>) for Riverboat shenanigans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T13:56:27-07:00","id":1121511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1121501#post1121501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Could you remember me how this was in the end ( this KS was like 2 years ago, right )? Cause Fallen Blossoms is single Hunter Era, not crossover one...</div> </div> </div> </div>Fallen Blossoms got voted in without having a gameline set for it, and then the devs assigned it Hunter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T13:57:03-07:00","id":1121512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1121507#post1121507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget, 1861 is when the American Civil War started. The Mississippi setting would be during the lead up to it, book-ending it with the Reconstruction Era we already got.<br /> <br /> Also, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maverick_(TV_series\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maverick_(TV_series</a>) and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maverick_(film\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maverick_(film</a>) for Riverboat shenanigans.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> More I think about it, the more I think it would be cool for this era to go to Changeling and have strong Underground Railroad elements (paralleling Changeling's own flight from the dogs of their masters). As unfortunate as its racial stereotypes (and character name) read today, obviously the plot of Huckelberry Finn sets a strong precedent for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T13:59:35-07:00","id":1121517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120287-de2-arthurian-discussion?p=1121468#post1121468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arthurian era strikes me as Mage/Changeling, because Merlin is an archetypal Wizard and a canon Archmaster in Mage books and references apparently exist in Changeling as well.<br /> <br /> However, if it wins, the Greco-Persian wars era seems to me as rather fitting for Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, this and this! I need my <b>(Were)Wolf</b> worshiping Spartans - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1003591-lycos-agema-vigilant-times-to-the-strongest\">like those</a>! Or let just <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> to send his fan Compact for <b>Hunter</b> then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b Plus spice it with showing the creation of Panscryptias cult for <b>Mage</b> ( can be simply crossover paragraph, I think ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T14:14:55-07:00","id":1121529,"title":"","content":"And now the blurbs: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Mississippi Steamboat Era, 1811 to 1861 C.E.</b><br /> <br /> In 1811, &quot;New Orleans&quot; the first Mississippi steamboat launched in Pittsburgh followed by more steamboats taking &quot;fast trips&quot; up and down the wide Mississippi river, pushing the boundaries of steam-powered technology while carrying coal, cotton, rice, timber, tobacco, and molasses. Throughout the 1800s, riverboats became a focal point, carrying needed goods from the Antebellum South to the North, attracting travelers, gamblers, and opportunists from St. Louis to New Orleans. In the Chronicles of Darkness, this era of prosperity was the turning point for its denizens--some who are eager to adapt and help plant the seeds of the Industrial Age, while others fight or flee out of fear for what's to come. <br /> <br /> <b>Necropolis of Hawara, Egypt, 1204-1604 B.C.E.</b> <br /> <br /> The fabled Necropolis of Hawara was the home to temple complexes, pyramids, and the Labyrinth of Hawara. Built by Amenemhet III during the Middle Kingdom, the Greek historian Herodotus later pinpoints the famous labyrinth's location &quot;near the place called the City of Crocodiles&quot;. Hawara or Het-waret, which is dedicated to the Egyptian god Sobek, was also home to artisans hired to paint funerary portraits and investors who owned shares in the necropolis and nearby burial grounds. This city of the dead, lorded over by the living, is home to many creatures in the Chronicles of Darkness who have their own agreements with the mortals above to retain a tenuous peace. <br /> <br /> <b>Greco-Persian Wars 499-449 B.C.E. </b><br /> <br /> The expanding Achaemenid Empire of Persia comes to blows with Greek city-states in a battle for control and expansion of territory. Time and time again, the great Achaemenid Empire of Persia fights, wins, and loses in city-states such as Athens, Sparta, Thespiae, and Thebes culminating in devastating battles such as the Battle of Thermopylae and Battle of Plataea which eventually end the conflict. Where there is war, however, there are sides to be chosen, and for creatures in the Chronicles of Darkness many are forced to choose between life and death in an age of warring fleets and shattered shields. </div> </div> </div>So with all that said...I'm going to lean towards Mississippi Steamboat and Greco-Persian Wars. Slightly more favorable leaning towards Mississippi Steamboat Era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"ke