":". 07-27-2017, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T14:50:55-07:00","id":1121557,"title":"","content":"Voted for the steamboats, because I was always interested in that part of my nation's history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2519-starglyte","name":"Starglyte","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T14:52:49-07:00","id":1121559,"title":"","content":"Disappointed that the Mississippi blurb doesn't mention slavery or escape there-from. That was the element that would interest me enough to change my support to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T14:55:40-07:00","id":1121561,"title":"","content":"&quot;Necropolis of Hawara, Egypt, 1204-1604 B.C.E. <br /> <br /> The fabled Necropolis of Hawara was the home to temple complexes, pyramids, and the Labyrinth of Hawara. Built by Amenemhet III during the Middle Kingdom, the Greek historian Herodotus later pinpoints the famous labyrinth's location &quot;near the place called the City of Crocodiles&quot;. Hawara or Het-waret, which is dedicated to the Egyptian god Sobek, was also home to artisans hired to paint funerary portraits and investors who owned shares in the necropolis and nearby burial grounds. This city of the dead, lorded over by the living, is home to many creatures in the Chronicles of Darkness who have their own agreements with the mortals above to retain a tenuous peace.&quot;<br /> <br /> Okay this won me over, I'm voting Hawara.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T15:02:54-07:00","id":1121562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1121534#post1121534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Steamboat is the objectively better choice. <br /> <br /> It's got steamboats, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly my perspective on the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T15:03:56-07:00","id":1121564,"title":"","content":"One thing I am really hoping they do more of in these is those quick one page blurbs of what at least the bulk of other splats could do in each era. They did it for some of the eras in the first dark ages but Id like to see it in every age if possible.<br /> <br /> Anyone else really like the idea of having interactions between the two lines as a major thing in each era? I like an intensive crossover more as a concept than having to write to complete narratives per era that you have to sacrifice some stuff in order to keep seperate. The idea of the round table being a coalition formed by two lines for example...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T15:30:16-07:00","id":1121579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1121564#post1121564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I am really hoping they do more of in these is those quick one page blurbs of what at least the bulk of other splats could do in each era. They did it for some of the eras in the first dark ages but Id like to see it in every age if possible.<br /> <br /> Anyone else really like the idea of having interactions between the two lines as a major thing in each era? I like an intensive crossover more as a concept than having to write to complete narratives per era that you have to sacrifice some stuff in order to keep seperate. The idea of the round table being a coalition formed by two lines for example...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm wirh you. I was really mad that most of the crossover Eras in DE1 didn't feel like crossover at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","valu