","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T20:33:54-07:00","id":1122188,"title":"","content":"I think the cost for that pledge was $1000, had to be quick, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T20:39:15-07:00","id":1122190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1122188#post1122188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the cost for that pledge was $1000, had to be quick, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe we can talk Rich into adding another one...<br /> <br /> What? I'm only half facetious. Rich is open to being convinced if someone has a good idea, the Kickstarter probably isn't going to get as many eras as planned, and it will give everything a boost in the final few days. Win for everyone!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T20:40:32-07:00","id":1122191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1122171#post1122171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, speaking as a Canadian, if you ask me to think of an ideallic American life in the early modern period, I will probably think of steamboat era Mississippi. That certainly doesn't mean that it was a perfect time period, very clearly was not because of the social forces at play, but I do think it has some nostalgia to it, especially thanks to Mark Twain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also Canadian here.<br /> To be honest, Huckleberry Finn horrified me, and was about as far from Idyllic as I can fathom. The choice of protagonist/perspective adds a layer of blitheness to the thing that makes it go down easier for the reader (probably specifically because Twain wanted to get it in the hands of young readers), but if you step back and examine the circumstances that are witnessed throughout it's a cesspool of a situation. If that is idyllic America, then America is one massively screwed up country.<br /> <br /> But yes, I'm also always game for more delicious Mummy or Mummy-adjacent content, so I'd be perfectly happy with seeing Hawara win too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9596-almacov","name":"Almacov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T20:40:48-07:00","id":1122192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1122190#post1122190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe we can talk Rich into adding another one...<br /> <br /> What? I'm only half facetious. Rich is open to being convinced if someone has a good idea, the Kickstarter probably isn't going to get as many eras as planned, and it will give everything a boost in the final few days. Win for everyone!</div> </div> </div> </div>It happened last time, I wouldn't count it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T20:45:08-07:00","id":1122193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1122192#post1122192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It happened last time, I wouldn't count it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>The X-factor is that there already is a Creator of Darkness this time and lasttime there wasn't. But having a rough idea of what RPG companies pay their freelancers and how Onyx compares to other companies, they should be breaking even on the pledge at a bare minimum. It wouldn't hurt to ask. Again. Although I pitched that idea last time, so maybe someone else could do it this time around,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T20:47:42-07:00","id":1122195,"title":"","content":"It's always possible someone will use the lower pledge to revitalize the Jazz Age era, that was the roaring twenties, and either it would be Mummy or someone might add Mummy to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T20:49:45-07:00","id":1122196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almacov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1122191#post1122191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also Canadian here.<br /> To be honest, Huckleberry Finn horrified me, and was about as far from Idyllic as I can fathom. The choice of protagonist/perspective adds a layer of blitheness to the thing that makes it go down easier for the reader (probably specifically because Twain wanted to get it in the hands of young readers), but if you step back and examine the circumstances that are witnessed throughout it's a cesspool of a situation. If that is idyllic America, then America is one massively screwed up country.<br /> <br /> But yes, I'm also always game for more delicious Mummy or Mummy-adjacent content, so I'd be perfectly happy with seeing Hawara win too.</div> </div> </div> </div>So that said, I think I only ever read Huck Finn as a kid, so that may be playing into it too. Definitely before I'd be able to comprehend how truely aweful it would be. But then again, said cesspool is at the root of every colonial nation/empire's &quot;glory days.&quot; They are all massively screwed up, us included.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T21:08:05-07:00","id":1122201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1122196#post1122196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then again, said cesspool is at the root of every colonial nation/empire's &quot;glory days.&quot; They are all massively screwed up, us included.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is almost always true, yeah.<br /> I see CofD as a really appealing lens to peel past that kind of &quot;glory days&quot; nostalgia with. That, and a lot of these unsettled periods produce really interesting folklore to draw from.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, hopefully we do see more add-ons and pledge types made available over the final stretch. The more of these settings get explored the better.<br /> <br /> In terms of game lines, I'd personally love to see more blue book style stuff sprinkled about. I'm particularly interested in weird creatures or phenomena that don't necessarily hew to a specific line.<br /> Hoping that Werewolf or Geist eras include ephemeral entities that would be right at home in a mortals game too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9596-almacov","name":"Almacov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T21:19:42-07:00","id":1122208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120106-seers-society?p=1120493#post1120493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My picks for Mississippi by the way are vampire/Changeling.<br /> <br /> Edit: and I just realized that was the Elizabethan duo, so another pairing would be viable to, but vampire gets you the New Orleans tie in, and Changeling works so well for exploring the struggles against American slavery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beside New Orleans now having both official settings for Vampire ( 1E core) and Changeling ( in 2E core), both are mentioned in Fearful Lesson from DEC 1. Not doing those as Vampire &amp; Changeling would be same travesty like not making Arthurs Britain in part for Mage. \u263a\ufe0f After reading pitches, I'm all in for Arthur's Mage &amp; Hunter Era!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T21:37:37-07:00","id":1122211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almacov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1122191#post1122191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also Canadian here.<br /> To be honest, Huckleberry Finn horrified me, and was about as far from Idyllic as I can fathom. The choice of protagonist/perspective adds a layer of blitheness to the thing that makes it go down easier for the reader (probably specifically because Twain wanted to get it in the hands of young readers), but if you step back and examine the circumstances that are witnessed throughout it's a cesspool of a situation. If that is idyllic America, then America is one massively screwed up country.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huck Finn wasn't supposed to be idyllic...it was a commentary on the hypocrisy of the South at the time and the slave culture going on there. Part of why Twain used Huck, a child, as the main character was because of the &quot;Emperor's New Clothes&quot; effect that children have, being able to bypass the societal moors already ingrained in adults to see things as they simply are. The moral climax of the book comes when Huck is torn between two moralities: the one adults try to teach him (that it's only right to report a runaway slave - what he's taught is the path to heaven) and the one that is innate to him and still accessible to his child's mind (that Jim is a good man and doesn't deserve his poor treatment - what Huck's taught is the path to hell), and he says &quot;All right then - I'll go to hell.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sure, there's plenty of description of the gorgeous Southern environment they're in, because it is a beautiful place. That was just part of the regionalist tradition in American literature. But the physical environment has nothing to do with the social story going on, to go with the theme of how things are portrayed versus how they really are underneath.<br /> <br /> All this said, I think it could definitely be an &quot;idyllic&quot; setting for CoD splats as looked through the same theme, being entities who portray themselves one way to most of the world, but underneath are something much stranger. The swamplands and forests of the South have always had their own unique, wonderful sense of mystery, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/2.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12708-chesh","name":"Chesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12708_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T21:46:55-07:00","id":1122214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almacov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1122191#post1122191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, Huckleberry Finn horrified me, and was about as far from Idyllic as I can fathom. The choice of protagonist/perspective adds a layer of blitheness to the thing that makes it go down easier for the reader (probably specifically because Twain wanted to get it in the hands of young readers), but if you step back and examine the circumstances that are witnessed throughout it's a cesspool of a situation. If that is idyllic America, then America is one massively screwed up country.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1122196#post1122196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So that said, I think I only ever read Huck Finn as a kid, so that may be playing into it too. Definitely before I'd be able to comprehend how truely aweful it would be. But then again, said cesspool is at the root of every colonial nation/empire's &quot;glory days.&quot; They are all massively screwed up, us included.</div> </div> </div> </div>...not 100% sure I'm qualified to talk about this since while I was born and raised in *a* southern part of the USA, I live in the *wrong* Southern part of the USA and on the wrong side of the Mississippi. But I did study the book in High School, so my memory isn't great but...<br /> <br /> Oh, I don't think Mark Twain intended for his depiction of the Southern States of the 19th century in his books to be a positive depiction of the place. In fact, it seems to be more of scathing critique of Southern society at that time. That the whole point of Huck and Jim's journey is discovering how, despite the claim that Southern white society is the inherently more superior and &quot;civilized&quot; society that is above whatever culture the black slaves brought in, that it is in fact VERY horrific with all the violence and hateful-ness, that it is anything but &quot;civilized&quot;.<br /> <br /> If anything, I'd be worried about any reader who takes the behavior of the characters that Huck and Jim meet as role models as &quot;true Southern way&quot; or whatever such nonsense.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, the crux of Huck's character arc is for him to accept the escaped slave Jim for what he is and as a normal human being just like him and not a slow-witted, superstitious and cowardly n**** that doesn't know better.<br /> <br /> Got my hard copy of Huck Finn stowed somewhere. When I get back home from OT, I'll flip through it if anything else comes to mind.<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: ...aaaand ninja'd by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12708-chesh\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12708_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12708\" data-vbnamecard=\"12708\">Chesh</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T21:51:02-07:00","id":1122216,"title":"","content":"@wyrdhamster<br /> I can certainly see the argument for choosing Vampire and Changeling to expand on what has all ready been established in New Orleans, but I don't really see it as a travesty if they choose to look at the river (and cities adjacent) through different lenses.<br /> When I read that they were considering a Mississippi Steamboat era my initial instinct was that they might be leaning Promethean because of how easily it would facilitate a roving, wandering chronicle, as well as some thematic resonance with the River of Death being a significant thing for the game. That line might be too obvious a fit though.<br /> I mean, if we're going with thematic resonance the Mississippi as a Nile analogue could be amusing for Mummy, but I'm not sure whether it would be a fit in other ways.<br /> We'll see what they decide on. I'm sure it will be interesting, whatever the case.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12708-chesh\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12708_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12708\" data-vbnamecard=\"12708\">Chesh</a> *&amp; @tasti man LH<br /> Yep. It's a smartly subversive book.<br /> To be clear, I was <i>questioning</i> the use of idyllic as a descriptor for the region in the era, and the idea that Twain's writing would have supported that nostalgia.<br /> The Mississippi at that time seems like a wonderful horror setting to me, and Twain did a great job illustrating some of what was scary about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9596,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9596-almacov","user":"Almacov","date":".  Clarification and acknowledging tasti man's post 07-29-2017, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9596-almacov","name":"Almacov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T21:59:50-07:00","id":1122218,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4418_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4418\" data-vbnamecard=\"4418\">tasti man LH</a> Gotta go fast <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/2.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12708-chesh","name":"Chesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12708_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T22:02:16-07:00","id":1122220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almacov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1122216#post1122216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@wyrdhamster<br /> I can certainly see the argument for choosing Vampire and Changeling to expand on what has all ready been established in New Orleans, but I don't really see it as a travesty if they choose to look at the river (and cities adjacent) through different lenses.<br /> When I read that they were considering a Mississippi Steamboat era my initial instinct was that they might be leaning Promethean because of how easily it would facilitate a roving, wandering chronicle, as well as some thematic resonance with the River of Death being a significant thing for the game. That line might be too obvious a fit though.<br /> I mean, if we're going with thematic resonance the Mississippi as a Nile analogue could be amusing for Mummy, but I'm not sure whether it would be a fit in other ways.<br /> We'll see what they decide on. I'm sure it will be interesting, whatever the case.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12708-chesh\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12708_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12708\" data-vbnamecard=\"12708\">Chesh</a> <br /> Yep. It's a smartly subversive book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Promethean/Mummy could be a very powerful exploration of slavery in this era. Promethean pilgrimages already came to my mind, but the abuses heaped o the Created due to Disquiet would be a strong analogue for the treatment and atitudes that slaveowners had for slaves. On the other hand, the Arisen were part of a callous and cruel Empire that had zero qualms about using and abusing human lives as property. There are a lot different types of internal conflicts Mummies could have in this era in recognizing or reaffirming their complicity in Irem's attrocities, or in their own continuing state of magical enslavement to the Judges. Plus each of the Guilds could have an interesting role to play.<br /> <br /> Ok, is my childhood filter on for Tom Sawyer as well? I don't remember that being subversive either, but now I'm questioning it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T22:11:36-07:00","id":1122226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1122220#post1122220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, is my childhood filter on for Tom Sawyer as well? I don't remember that being subversive either, but now I'm questioning it.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest it's been so long since I read Tom Sawyer, if ever I did, that I don't feel qualified to speak on it. I need to get around to that, given the effect Huck Finn had on me.<br /> <br /> Mississippi Mummy could be a really pleasant surprise. Again, I can't see myself ever complaining about more Mummy content...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9596-almacov","name":"Almacov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T22:17:03-07:00","id":1122228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1122220#post1122220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, is my childhood filter on for Tom Sawyer as well? I don't remember that being subversive either, but now I'm questioning it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huck Finn was a direct attack on the South's culture. Tom Sawyer was more of a personal growth journey with the criticisms of social institutions coming through more subtly. There's still plenty of shade thrown at everything from law to the church, but whereas one of the main messages of Huck Finn was anti-slavery, the main message of Tom Sawyer is how he develops from a child to join this flawed adult world. His is more an Alice in Wonderland style adventure in that aspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/2.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12708-chesh","name":"Chesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12708_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T22:20:31-07:00","id":1122229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1122228#post1122228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huck Finn was a direct attack on the South's culture. Tom Sawyer was more of a personal growth journey with the criticisms of social institutions coming through more subtly. There's still plenty of shade thrown at everything from law to the church, but whereas one of the main messages of Huck Finn was anti-slavery, the main message of Tom Sawyer is how he develops from a child to join this flawed adult world. His is more an Alice in Wonderland style adventure in that aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that must be more what I'm thinking of when I think of this era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T22:30:57-07:00","id":1122230,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, Disquiet would be difficult to deal with on a steamboat, and there's the unfortunate fact that if you were a person of color on a steamboat, you were likely a slave and never able to leave said steamboat. And as a slave you would also likely be forced to work the steam furnace, and be the first casualty in the event of an explosion. Unless you were a Native American, where the steamer was just used to remove you from your lands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-29-2017, 01:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T22:31:50-07:00","id":1122231,"title":"","content":"I'm semi-hyped for Arthurian Mage/Hunter - finally my fan Legacy <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/92189-european-knight-legacy?p=95253#post95253\">Order of Round Table</a> would come from Hunter Compact working under Merlin! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T22:40:40-07:00","id":1122233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sultana_%28steamboat%29\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Ill-fated_Sultana%2C_Helena%2C_Arkansas%2C_April_27%2C_1865.jpg/1280px-Ill-fated_Sultana%2C_Helena%2C_Arkansas%2C_April_27%2C_1865.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sultana_%28steamboat%29\" target=\"_blank\"> Sultana (steamboat) - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sultana_%28steamboat%29\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sultana_%28steamboat%29 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;<i><b>Sultana</b></i> was a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mississippi_River\" target=\"_blank\">Mississippi River</a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paddlewheeler\" target=\"_blank\">side-wheel</a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steamboat\" target=\"_blank\">steamboat</a>. On April 27, 1865, the boat exploded in the worst <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_maritime_disasters\" target=\"_blank\">maritime disaster</a> in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States\" target=\"_blank\">United States</a> history. She was designed with a capacity of only 376 passengers, but she was carrying 2,155 when three of the boat's four boilers exploded and she burned to the waterline and sank near <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memphis,_Tennessee\" target=\"_blank\">Memphis, Tennessee</a>, killing 1,192 passengers.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, I'm not saying there are plenty of things about the Steamboat Era for Sin-Eaters...but there totally are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/2.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12708-chesh","name":"Chesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12708_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T23:27:00-07:00","id":1122243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1122220#post1122220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Promethean/Mummy could be a very powerful exploration of slavery in this era. Promethean pilgrimages already came to my mind, but the abuses heaped o the Created due to Disquiet would be a strong analogue for the treatment and atitudes that slaveowners had for slaves. On the other hand, the Arisen were part of a callous and cruel Empire that had zero qualms about using and abusing human lives as property. There are a lot different types of internal conflicts Mummies could have in this era in recognizing or reaffirming their complicity in Irem's attrocities, or in their own continuing state of magical enslavement to the Judges. Plus each of the Guilds could have an interesting role to play.<br /> <br /> Ok, is my childhood filter on for Tom Sawyer as well? I don't remember that being subversive either, but now I'm questioning it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember with the Arisen too that they are both master and slave; their callousness towards mortal servants and archaic social values do nothing to disguise the fact that they are dehumanized tools for those they serve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T23:56:43-07:00","id":1122247,"title":"","content":"Just realized the winning polls have a Disney theme to them. Pirates of the Caribbean. Sword in the Stone. Steamboat Willie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join 