custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T19:06:53-07:00","id":1124569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1124526#post1124526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Totally want Golden Age of Science Fiction for Deviant &amp; Promethean. Would be perfect fit!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Deviant and Demon could also be a good fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T19:09:18-07:00","id":1124571,"title":"","content":"I'd really like a Promethean/Demon crossover that explores the missions of the of Qashmallim and Angels crossing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T19:10:46-07:00","id":1124572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1124560#post1124560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the record the real Golden Age of Sci Fi was the 90's in my opinion. DS9, Voyager, TNG, Stargate SG-1, ect..., and so on, before Reality Television took took the Golden Age out back and killed it..</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of fiction 'Golden Age' doesn't necessarily mean the time when it was most popular, which would be its own debate anyway.<br /> <br /> The Golden Age of Comics was pre-WW2 but it's still the heritage of the Silver Age that we all think of when we think of classic comic book super-heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T19:17:23-07:00","id":1124577,"title":"","content":"Is it weird I almost hope Hawara doesn't focus on mummy? It may be my favorite gameline, but I feel it would suit things better as plothooks and antagonists for other games in this era. Most mummy Sts, especially with the expanded stuff in DAC and Rio, could probably use just a few little blurbs to flesh out this era, while Hunter, Vampire, and Gist would be really really good for this era. Mage might have gotten Pirates, for historical events. Mummies.. well,, I'd rather here how others in the era deal with cults and maybe one or two ''outsider perspectives'' for a mummy antagonist than see more PC mummy stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T19:17:58-07:00","id":1124578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1124572#post1124572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of fiction 'Golden Age' doesn't necessarily mean the time when it was most popular, which would be its own debate anyway.<br /> <br /> The Golden Age of Comics was pre-WW2 but it's still the heritage of the Silver Age that we all think of when we think of classic comic book super-heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's messed up, the Golden Age is supposed to be the best stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T19:21:28-07:00","id":1124580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1124577#post1124577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it weird I almost hope Hawara doesn't focus on mummy? It may be my favorite gameline, but I feel it would suit things better as plothooks and antagonists for other games in this era. Most mummy Sts, especially with the expanded stuff in DAC and Rio, could probably use just a few little blurbs to flesh out this era, while Hunter, Vampire, and Gist would be really really good for this era. Mage might have gotten Pirates, for historical events. Mummies.. well,, I'd rather here how others in the era deal with cults and maybe one or two ''outsider perspectives'' for a mummy antagonist than see more PC mummy stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div> I actually kind of like Changeling for this era, curious as to what kind of court system they could come up with for ancient Egypt (although wonders of the world may cover that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T19:23:20-07:00","id":1124581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1124563#post1124563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Why did I click? I knew what it was, so why did I bother?</div> </div> </div> </div> M\u00e5 wow ha ha ha ha ha ha ha!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T19:24:44-07:00","id":1124582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1124577#post1124577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it weird I almost hope Hawara doesn't focus on mummy? It may be my favorite gameline, but I feel it would suit things better as plothooks and antagonists for other games in this era. Most mummy Sts, especially with the expanded stuff in DAC and Rio, could probably use just a few little blurbs to flesh out this era, while Hunter, Vampire, and Gist would be really really good for this era. Mage might have gotten Pirates, for historical events. Mummies.. well,, I'd rather here how others in the era deal with cults and maybe one or two ''outsider perspectives'' for a mummy antagonist than see more PC mummy stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not weird, I agree. There's also the Sophis Ascends book I already mentioned, which has three Egyptian Dark Eras for Mummy.<br /> <br /> I suspect this has been thought of by the developers, however. One of them was a writer for Sothis Ascends.<br /> <br /> In the end we'll see what's what. I'm just hoping they announce the game lines at some point soon. After would make sense, so people can't withdraw their pledge if they don't like one, though I think RichT is forgiving about that kind of stuff. But soon after would be good, waiting months to find out if I can look forward to putting something in the game I'm running or want to run would have great impact on how eager I am for the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T19:36:49-07:00","id":1124588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1124578#post1124578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's messed up, the Golden Age is supposed to be the best stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's the era that birthed the tropes the era you're referring to was replicating. I love DS9, but it was not more influential to science fiction than the works of Asimov or Bradbury.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T21:44:52-07:00","id":1124615,"title":"","content":"Oh, we crossed $56k.<br /> <br /> Granted, these Eras are going to have their work cut out for them. Who knows if they even can reach $60k.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T21:49:49-07:00","id":1124616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1124304#post1124304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I think I've got my potential expansions winnowed down a bit.<br /> <br /> - French Revolution Mummy<br /> - Western Front Promethean<br /> - Seven Wonders Mummy<br /> - Pirate Hunter<br /> - 1001 Nights Mage<br /> - Arthurian Demon (if Mage/Changeling)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Starglyte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1124550#post1124550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pirate Hunter and 1001 Nights Mage sound cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconding on both of those options here, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> . <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-04-2017, 12:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T21:56:53-07:00","id":1124617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1124615#post1124615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, we crossed $56k.<br /> <br /> Granted, these Eras are going to have their work cut out for them. Who knows if they even can reach $60k.</div> </div> </div> </div>Written 6 hours ago:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1124504#post1124504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it? In last 3 hours we were getting 500$ - so I say if the funding will be at this pace, we will hit at least this Stretch Goal. ( We are waaaayyyy more than 30 hours till end of Kickstarter. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</div> </div> </div> </div>We got 800$ in next 6 hours then - and we still are 34 hours to end. I'm rather confident we will get S-F or Ireland Era - but they probably be last ones. Still, it's all educated guess for now...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-04-2017, 01:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T00:26:28-07:00","id":1124644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1124304#post1124304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I think I've got my potential expansions winnowed down a bit.<br /> <br /> - French Revolution Mummy<br /> - Western Front Promethean<br /> - Seven Wonders Mummy<br /> - Pirate Hunter<br /> - 1001 Nights Mage<br /> - Arthurian Demon (if Mage/Changeling)</div> </div> </div> </div>Love the possibility of Western Front Promethean and Pirate Hunter.<br /> <br /> I voted Medieval Ireland for the new poll, but I'm totally fine if Science Fiction takes it. Seems like another possible Deviant era to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13726-world-s-first-ghost","name":"World's First Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T04:25:18-07:00","id":1124690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1124588#post1124588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's the era that birthed the tropes the era you're referring to was replicating. I love DS9, but it was not more influential to science fiction than the works of Asimov or Bradbury.</div> </div> </div> </div> Star Trek as a singular entity absolutely is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T04:47:39-07:00","id":1124694,"title":"","content":"We are over 57 000$ on Kickstarter right now - We can do (at least ) this Streach Goal! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> In the Poll Age of S-F have 37% and Ireland or Mali are having 32% and 31%, respectively - on 300 votes cast.<br /> <br /> Lasl Egyptian Era was unlocked with almost 900 votes cast, so we are in 1/3 now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T05:19:17-07:00","id":1124706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1124690#post1124690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Star Trek as a singular entity absolutely is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Debatable. Much of Star Trek was inspired by earlier media.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T05:54:56-07:00","id":1124717,"title":"","content":"I really want Mali, especially since it was my suggestion, put I'll be pretty stoked if I get to see Asimov in CofD. While seeing the Irish Kingdoms and Hiberno-Norse would be cool, the Viking Era already gave us Ireland, so for diversity's sake, I'm rooting for the other two.<br /> <br /> $2901 to go...<br /> <br /> Is there anyone who can upgrade to that high end pledge? That would really help us out down the stretch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T06:59:04-07:00","id":1124744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1124569#post1124569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Deviant and Demon could also be a good fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. That said, I'd be kind of disappointed if it went to Demon. It's already fairly simple to take a science fiction approach to Demon, so going with that one strikes me as low-hanging fruit. It's not that I don't think it would be awesome, but I'd prefer to see something a little less expected for that one. Personally I'd like to see Changeling for that one, but I'm biased, so take that for what it's worth. I'd still want to see Deviant for it, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T07:10:37-07:00","id":1124748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1124304#post1124304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I think I've got my potential expansions winnowed down a bit.<br /> <br /> - French Revolution Mummy<br /> - Western Front Promethean<br /> - Seven Wonders Mummy<br /> - Pirate Hunter<br /> - 1001 Nights Mage<br /> - Arthurian Demon (if Mage/Changeling)<br /> <br /> There's actually quite a bit more thought I've out into those, but I don't have time to transcribe it right now. As always, open to suggestions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no other suggestions to offer until they reveal the lines for the stretch goals, but of those that you've put forth here, Pirate Hunter, Western Front Promethean, or the Mummy options would be the ones that I'd find most interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T08:01:55-07:00","id":1124777,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering about Medieval Ireland. There will be quite a bit of overlap with the Viking Werewolf era from DE1, won't it? Since that focused a lot on the battle of Dublin, and the situations around it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T08:06:55-07:00","id":1124779,"title":"","content":"Just voted.<br /> <br /> It is now 138 for Ireland, 132 for Sci-fi.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T08:16:30-07:00","id":1124785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1124690#post1124690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Star Trek as a singular entity absolutely is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in terms of establishing the broader genre, no it isn't.<br /> <br /> In terms of introducing it to mass audiences, plus other social influences on television, sure. But the forging of space opera as a genre, the use of artificial intelligence to explore questions of identity, space aliens used to deconstructs racism and xenophobia, etc etc - that all originates guys like Asimov and Bradbury.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T09:40:40-07:00","id":1124809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1124748#post1124748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have no other suggestions to offer until they reveal the lines for the stretch goals, but of those that you've put forth here, Pirate Hunter, Western Front Promethean, or the Mummy options would be the ones that I'd find most interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>So here are some expansions on those. I haven't written up the Arthurian one yet since we don't know the games, but suffice to say, Fate Arcana/Pacts/Pledgecrafting would be central to it. Bonus points for being a late Roman era, since the Romans always took their oaths super seriously.<br /> <br /> <b>French Revolution</b> (VtR/MtC/DtD)<br /> In this era, immortal, ancient, and inhuman beings stalk the streets driven by all too human conflict. Vampires and Mummies are both ancient, relying on old, conservative power structures... until they start to crumble. How do these undead immortals relate to each other? What is the relationship between the forces that sustain them, Sekhem and Vitae? In the upheaval of the Revolution, both Demons and the God-Machine take advantage of the chaos to alter and twist Infrastructure, but these alterations are not taken kindly by the geometrically-inclined Arisen. The God-Machine may be an ancient and unknowable horror, but so are the Judges and the Mummies themselves as they strike out from their fortress in Louvre palace. It is up to the Unchained whether they should trust this enemy of their enemy... or whether this is just more competition. Does the Aether that Infrastructure generates have any relation to the Lifeweb of the Mummies? Can Infrastructure influence the channeling of Heka? Do Demons stand to gain anything from Relic Architecture and the Tombs of Mummies?<br /> <br /> <b>Great War</b> (WtF/PtC/GtSE)<br /> Promethean walk the land and new lineage is born out of the gas attacks, starting at Ypres, but they are not the only Created to create Wastelands in no man's lands. The Ulgan across France, Belgium, and Germany can sense the turmoil that the spirits are in because of the war and urge every throng they cross to come to the aid of the Werewolves desperately trying to keep them in check, even if that means crossing into the Shadow. Meanwhile, Prometheans well on their pilgrimage feel stirrings from the Underworld, and feel compelled to journey physically to the Rivers of Death to investigate, even as Sin-Eaters do the same. As the Created journey farther afield into the supernatural realms, they find the Shadow and Underworld roiling in unexpected ways, and must learn how to interact with ghosts, spirits, and cthonians... and how their disquiet impacts each one. <br /> <br /> <b>Seven Wonders</b> (PtC/CtL/MtC)<br /> As Promethens, Mummies, and Changelings are all drawn towards the greatest monuments of their times, they all ask themselves how did they get here? Mummies say that it was Fate, somehow intoning it so solemnly, you know that the first letter is a capital. Changelings say that it was the Wyrd, and the stories-oathes bound within. Prometheans say it was the Principle, and that their Pilgrimage demands it. How do the Wyrd, the Principle, and Fate relate to each other? Are they reflections of one another viewed from different lenses, or are they separate forces working at cross-purposes? Does the power of Azoth relate at all to life-giving Sekhem? Could a mummy eat away at the Divine Fire, or will they be burned from within? And is there some fundamental connection between the Glamour that Changelings harvest and the Pillars that keep Mummies standing?<br /> <br /> <b>1001 Nights</b> (VtR/MtA/BtP)<br /> It is a time of fables, stories, and high adventure! It is also a time of science, discovery, and exploration! It is inevitable that the two would collide. In this age, Ibn Batuta travels to far off lands, bringing back stories of horrors and wonders from the edge of ten Muslim world. Ibn Sina, the great scientist in the East or West prior to the Renaissance, compiled the medical knowledge of China, India, Persia, and Greece using poetic verse. Vampires, Mages, and Beast all hunger for different things; blood, knowledge, and fear; but those goals overlap and interlock. Thyrusus and Moros Mages collaborate with Vampire scientists to study the properties Vitae and understand the Kindred's undead condition. Obrimos and Acanthus enjoy the Islamic Neoplatonic revitalization, applying the idea of ideal forms to stories, and working with Beasts to track the spread and changes of the 1001 Nights through the Astral Realms. From the Nizari Ismaili State the Mastigos Hassan-I-Sabah and Nizari Quhistani, watch as their people are slandered as drug addicts and hedonists, when really they are farmers and philosophers. With the Fatimids, Ayuubids, and Mongols pressing in on them, and Kindred infiltrating the Syrian stronghold Masayaf, they have better things to worry about than setting the record straight, allowing the Assassin Legends to take root.<br /> <br /> <b>Pirates</b> (MtA/HtV/GtSE)<br /> Pirates! What's worse than pirates? Monster pirates. The British started this whole mess with their privateers. Our Spanish compact will crush any pirate or privateer they meet on the high seas root out the heretics among them. The Mughal Emperor Aurangzeb commanded us to rid the Indian Ocean of this plague of thieves before he died. If the pirates traffic with ghostly jinn to avoid death, we will hunt them down again! Pirate witches come north from New York to hide their treasures and ghastly rites in Nova Scotia. We will see them tarred and feathered, hanging from the gallows! All of these self righteous Compacts are fools! Why do they think we built a Pirate Nation in Madagascar? Because society is corrupt with monsters. Our Conspiracy of monster hunting keeps us free. Look at the these other who say they hold the Vigil? The Council of Bones and the Lucifuge? The Ageis Kai Doru and the Mallius Malficarum? The Acheron Group? They all pervert themselves by using magic to hunt monsters. Witches can see the realms from which they draw their magic, and so turn it against them. On Madagascar, we made no such mistake. <br /> <br /> Right now I'm leading towards Mage 1001 Nights, but as always, I am open to suggestions, and may change my mind. Also, if other expansion backers are lurking here, you are welcome, nay encouraged, to steal what I've written for your own pitches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a