during the Italian Renaissance, the Voynich Manuscript is a cryptic codex filled with wondrous illustrations that have yet to be fully identified. Written in an indecipherable language, its folios depict herbal, astronomical, biological, cosmological, and pharmaceutical illustrations, along with several recipes. While the codex's many secrets have yet to be unraveled in the modern era, in the Chronicles of Darkness the codex's creation sits at the center of a maelstrom. On the one hand, the codex represents a unique collaborative effort to collate evidence of the supernatural and natural worlds. On the other, there are many creatures who believe this work acts as proof of their existence and abilities, and would do anything to suppress its creation.<br /> <br /> Wild West, 1865 to 1895 <br /> The Old West is marked by prospectors and scouts, gangs of outlaws and gunfighters, lawmen and gamblers, and, of course, cowboys. Dotted with small towns and historic passages west, the Old West has been romanticized into an American ideal: manifest destiny. Life on the mythological frontier is far removed from its historical roots, however, and the propaganda sent back east doesn't match the reality. In the Chronicles of Darkness, the Wild West takes on an even darker shape, as its denizens struggle to understand the rapidly changing landscape and the problems new settlers bring.<br /> <br /> Edit: Damn. Voynich's description almost wants me to change my mine. Almost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a hre