</a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T22:36:01-07:00","id":1138505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1138452#post1138452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I guess it's good Voynich Manuscript didn't take a slot, because the whole premise of the era would be ruined now if it had... <a href=\"https://www.the-tls.co.uk/articles/public/voynich-manuscript-solution/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.the-tls.co.uk/articles/p...ript-solution/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>never trust an article before other people put it to the test. The manuscript has been &quot;solved&quot; a number of times in the past, after all. I'm not saying that this may not be the &quot;right&quot; solution, but it is far from saying &quot;the mystery is solved once and for all&quot;. There are a lot of steps to go through before the solution would be verified, and even then we could still use the fact that the CofD in not exactly our world, and that things are different in there- so no, it doesn't really harm the premise of that Era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T06:59:17-07:00","id":1138567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1138427#post1138427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the choices are all unexpected, then my guess is all of the lines are Mummy content <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Every dark era is Mummy content!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T07:28:13-07:00","id":1138574,"title":"","content":"Oh, and by the by, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> 's pitches are fricking awesome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T05:49:08-07:00","id":1139418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1138505#post1138505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">never trust an article before other people put it to the test. The manuscript has been &quot;solved&quot; a number of times in the past, after all. I'm not saying that this may not be the &quot;right&quot; solution, but it is far from saying &quot;the mystery is solved once and for all&quot;. There are a lot of steps to go through before the solution would be verified, and even then we could still use the fact that the CofD in not exactly our world, and that things are different in there- so no, it doesn't really harm the premise of that Era.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://arstechnica.com/science/2017/09/experts-are-extremely-dubious-about-the-voynich-solution/\" target=\"_blank\">Guess what.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T12:41:10-07:00","id":1150418,"title":"","content":"Backerkit surveys have gone out. I'm hoping that means that the full Table of Contents gets announced soon, because believe it or not, even I'm tired of typing [REDACTED], and I really want to talk about [REDACTED], [REDACTED], and [REDACTED].","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T14:18:31-07:00","id":1150467,"title":"","content":"I expect there's going to be considerable amount of whining over one of the choices so it would be nice to be able to get that out of the forum ahead of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T17:59:35-07:00","id":1150511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150467#post1150467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I expect there's going to be considerable amount of whining over one of the choices so it would be nice to be able to get that out of the forum ahead of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. If I'm thinking of the same one as you, I think it will catch people off guard, but that its a good fit once everyone gets to take a closer look. I would have done it slightly differently if it was my call, but its not, and otherwise I was pretty bang on with my predictions. For those of you who aren't nofather, said predictions were not posted in this forum, so take anything I said earlier in this thread with a huge grain of salt. I'm not talking about them. <br /> <br /> Mostly, I just want to not have to talk like I'm a James Bond spy anymore. This saying something while saying absolutely nothing gig is tiring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T11:13:41-07:00","id":1150708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150418#post1150418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Backerkit surveys have gone out. I'm hoping that means that the full Table of Contents gets announced soon, because believe it or not, even I'm tired of typing [REDACTED], and I really want to talk about [REDACTED], [REDACTED], and [REDACTED].</div> </div> </div> </div>And as of <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/chronicles-of-darkness-dark-eras-2/posts/2018962\" target=\"_blank\">the latest update</a>, we have it:<br /> <br /> <b>Dark Eras 2: Table of Contents</b><br /> French Revolution \u2013 Vampire The Requiem /Demon The Descent /Mummy The Curse<br /> Great War/Western Front \u2013 Geist The Sin-Eaters /Werewolf The Forsaken /Promethean The Created<br /> Light of the Sun \u2013 Deviant The Renegade /Mage The Awakening /Demon<br /> Seven Wonders \u2013 Changeling The Lost /Promethean<br /> Last Imperials \u2013 Mummy /Hunter The Vigil<br /> One Thousand and One Nights \u2013 Beast The Primordial /Vampire<br /> Golden Age of Piracy \u2013 Mage /Geist<br /> King Arthur\u2019s Britannia \u2013 Hunter/Changeling /Vampire<br /> Necropolis of Hawara \u2013 Promethean /Beast /Werewolf<br /> Golden Age of Sci Fi \u2013 Deviant /Werewolf<br /> Scandinavian Witch Trials (1450-1750) \u2013 Mummy /Geist<br /> Wild West \u2013 Changeling/Mage<br /> Empire of Mali \u2013 Hunter/Demon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T11:19:03-07:00","id":1150710,"title":"","content":"I fist pumped when I saw Promethean as part of the Great War. So happy.<br /> <br /> But also Beast gets a second era so I'm also happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T11:37:13-07:00","id":1150715,"title":"","content":"Niiiiiice.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, no Mage for Britannia. On the other hand, people are still getting some Changeling and Hunter on top of Vampires.<br /> <br /> Hawara I am a bit disappointed that there's no Geist for it...but Promethean/Beast/Werewolf is certainly an unexpected but interesting choice.<br /> <br /> I am super stoked for Golden Age of Sci-Fi. Deviant is a bit of a gimme, I admit, but Werewolf on the other hand should be interesting. Just the idea of Uratha suddenly having to deal with spirits that resemble extraterrestrial aliens should make for some fun times. And of course, the idigam's connection to the moon and therefore space could be interesting (despite it still being several decades before the moon landing).<br /> <br /> Unexpected choice being the Scandinavian Witch Trials with Mummy/Geist...unfortunately I don't know a whole lot about it. Curious to see how that goes. Although the interplay between eternal servants that cannot die versus mortals that get a second chance at life after dying could be cool.<br /> <br /> Also, thank you to whatever beautiful bastard brought back Wild West. Changeling/Mage, for me, is certainly an unexpected combination but I'm curious to see how that pans out.<br /> <br /> Empire of Mali, well at least a non-Euro-centric Era was added. My knowledge of it only extends to the legend of Sundiata, but I'm curious at the rest nonetheless.<br /> <br /> (and also uber sad Mississippi Steamboats didn't make the cut)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 10-18-2017, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T11:43:30-07:00","id":1150719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150708#post1150708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">King Arthur\u2019s Britannia \u2013 Hunter/Changeling /Vampire</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/meme/images/8/81/Genius-meme.png/revision/latest?cb=20140626182735\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T11:43:34-07:00","id":1150720,"title":"","content":"I got Hawara right! Yay!<br /> <br /> Also, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a>, I must say you have misled me! Arthur's Era is the most expected thing I could have imagined (not that I have something against seeing the potential of seeing the Weihan Cynn again, or having a new Hunter Era), and Sci Fi Deviant is way too expected (even though my secondary guess did included Werewolf, so I'm half half right- one quarter right? Who knows?).<br /> <br /> More seriously, I am happy seeing Mummy in the French Revolution (the Mummy/Mage crossover sounded interesting but getting the Tenth Choir compensate for it). Promethean in the Great War means we get our Chemical Weapon Lineage, which means we only need a biological one to complete the HAZMAT set, which is also good. Demon in the Scientific Revolution also has potential, for obvious reasons. I'm not sure about Beast in Hawara, simply because I lack a clear vision of how that Era would be special for them. I'm a bit annoyed that there is no Geist in the Wild West, but Hunter/Demon in the Empire of Mali is awesome enough for two Eras. The Scandinavian Witch Hunts sounds interesting, and Mummy/Geist crossover also sounds great, but I have some difficulties at overlapping the two pictures one over the other (I can rationalize myself how it makes sense, but it is hard for me to actually see it). As I understand that this is the newly created Dark Era which was chosen, could we now know which one didn't got i?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T11:58:09-07:00","id":1150723,"title":"","content":"Yes! We finally can talk about it!<br /> <br /> So the era I'm not sure about how people will react to is Wild West. I was very surprised that it got paired with Mage and Changeling, but the more I think about it, the more I think those are nice fits to the themes of the West in those eras. I also hope we see a bit of the Canadian West too, specifically the Red River Rebellion. Also, this era matches the last decades of the Nameless War, which could be interesting. I think that's the same one nofather is talking about, but I'm not sure. <br /> <br /> I am very pumped for Werewolf/Deviant Golden Age of Sci-Fi. I was half-hoping that my suggestion of Mummy would get used, but Werewolf was my second choice for that era and Deviant is the obvious choice to go with it.<br /> <br /> I am beyond happy that Mali made it in and I've paired it with Demon multiple times when suggesting it all the way to DE1's Kickstarer, so the Hunter/Demon pairing is fantastic. <br /> <br /> I'm not going to be the one to spill the beans on Scandinavian Witch Trials, but it is going to be awesome. I was kinda lukewarm on the idea since we already have a lot of Europe and we've covered it in both Dark Eras books (Doubting Souls and likely Light of the Sun), but then the backer paired it with Mummy, which was totally unexpected and awesome. The fact that Monica, Matthew, Meghan then tossed us Mummy fans a bone by pairing it with Geist is just icing on the cake. <br /> <br /> Also, since it was asked for, here is the original era pitch that was <b>NOT </b>used. Once Deviant comes out, I'd love to do a write-up of this one. I've done some minor edits for clarity and grammar. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u><b><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Norwegian Crusade(1107-1113)</span></span></b></u><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This era focuses on the crusade undertaken by King Sigurd Jorsalfar the Crusader, who took 5000 men and traveled down from Norway to England, Galicia, Al-Andalus, the Balearic Islands, Sicily before finally reaching Outremere. So not only can we look at the societal impact of the crusades in Europe, while also studying this specific campaign, we can also look at the culture of Al-Andalus and the Crusader states. It gives us a wide cultural and historic basis to press into the chapter, but not so big that we are trying to examine one of the biggest events in Medieval history as a whole. We can also look at the Byzantine Empire before it fell and the crusaders journey home through the mainland of Europe. All in all, this gives us an equally exciting and varied plate to study as in the previous pitch.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As for the gameline i would like to suggest Deviant the Renegades, as i seem to recall that they at least for now do not have any era prior to the early modern one. So through this we can examine the Renegades in a pre modern era, and through the lens of several cultures and perspectives. </span></span> </div> </div> </div>Hawara was unexpected for me and it was one of the eras that I thought people would be pleasantly surprised by. Promethean/Beast was the original combo, then one of the expansion backers tossed Werewolf into the fray. <br /> <br /> Arthur is the other one that I could see putting people's noses a bit out of joint due to the absence of Mage, but I think that means Merlin will be out of focus, which is fine by me. This was originally Changeling/Hunter, then Vampire got added into the fray. It is going to be balling!<br /> <br /> Adding Demon to Light of the Sun was another expansion that was on my shortlist and I really hope we get to find out what Demons are like under Mage Sight. <br /> <br /> French Revolution Mummy speaks for itself. Infrastructure vs Relic Arcitecture. Let's do this!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150710#post1150710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fist pumped when I saw Promethean as part of the Great War. So happy.<br /> <br /> But also Beast gets a second era so I'm also happy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its a bit bittersweet for me. I REALLY wanted to add Mage to 1001 Nights, but I also really wanted to add Promethean to Great War, so it works out in the end. Ironically, the only era that I didn't correctly predict before Monica announced the TofC to the expansion backers was my own (I didn't try to predict line for Wild West or Mali though). Also, everything except adding Vampire to Arthur was on my shortlist of expansion when the kickstarter ended, so I really have zero grounds to complain about and am overwhelmingly happy with how things have turned out as a result. I think we are going to get some really cool stuff out of Great War too. I specifically wrote in some major crossover points for Ulgan/Forsaken stories and an exploration of the Rivers of Death. <br /> <br /> Also, if anyone is interested, I did some breakdowns, and this is the most even spread of eras it could possibly be. Each gameline got three eras, barring Beast and Deviant, who each got two. Both are relatively new games and Beast has the most upcoming products of any game, so that makes sense. Each game also gets a fairly even number of crossovers. Vampire and Demon get five each, Promethean and Werewolf get four plus an extra crossover with each other, Beast and Deviant gets three, and everyone else gets four. I'm really amazed at how equitable the Devs managed to be with this book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T12:23:48-07:00","id":1150727,"title":"","content":"Without wanting to troll or being offensive, I don't see any logic in the choice of these combos. (Non-mage Camelot is especially hurting me but it's not the weirdest one).<br /> Has anyone here any clues on the reasons behind these splats - eras choices? I'm just curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T12:37:01-07:00","id":1150730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suleri Drals</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150727#post1150727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without wanting to troll or being offensive, I don't see any logic in the choice of these combos. (Non-mage Camelot is especially hurting me but it's not the weirdest one).</div> </div> </div> </div>The three-gameline eras are due to backers. Vampires in Arthurian time are from me, for instance. Previously it was Changeling and Hunter. Vampire has many ties to Arthurian times and as I said in my pitch, the muddled legends and facts of the time are a prime example of how vampires meddle with history.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T12:43:33-07:00","id":1150733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150715#post1150715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Niiiiiice.<br /> <br /> Also, thank you to whatever beautiful bastard brought back Wild West. Changeling/Mage, for me, is certainly an unexpected combination but I'm curious to see how that pans out.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was supposed to be my era suggestion. As happy as I am to have Wild West as a setting, it's a little disheartening to see the focus of it be centered on splats I have no interest in. Neither I nor the other era resurrector had any say in what splats we wanted for our eras, otherwise I'd have pitched something for Geist or Promethean. Wild West was also my second choice, after Mississippi Steamboats, so I'm also a little disappointed that such a unique era in American history doesn't get to be explored.<br /> <br /> But in the end, as long as there are people who get to benefit from my pledge, I can't be too upset. I'm very excited for the other eras, especially the Promethean add-on to the Great War. I'm looking forward to see the final results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13726-world-s-first-ghost","user":"World's First Ghost","date":". 10-18-2017, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13726-world-s-first-ghost","name":"World's First Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T12:46:05-07:00","id":1150735,"title":"","content":"Mostly I want to see that Great War lineage the 2nd edition Promethean core book alluded to <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T12:46:41-07:00","id":1150736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suleri Drals</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150727#post1150727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without wanting to troll or being offensive, I don't see any logic in the choice of these combos. (Non-mage Camelot is especially hurting me but it's not the weirdest one).<br /> Has anyone here any clues on the reasons behind these splats - eras choices? I'm just curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can touch on some of it since I've know about the final contents for the last three weeks, so I've had some time to process. One thing to keep in mind is that some of the choices were dictated by what the backers who added something to the book (like your's truly) wanted to add. <br /> <br /> For Arthurian Britannia, there is actually a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120287-de2-arthurian-discussion\">seven page discussion thread</a> on this very forum where people discuss the merits of each of the three chosen eras, as well as Arthurian Mage. I will let <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> speak to Vampire in this era, since that was his expansion, but I can speak to Hunter and Changeling. <br /> <br /> <b><u>Hunter</u></b>: Knights of the Round Table is probably all I have to say. Yes, it is anachronistic for the time period, but if you are going to reconstruct the Round Table in a post-Roman Britain, Hunter is definitely the way to go. That would also allow us to see what the Compacts and Conspiracies of late Rome were like, which I for one and very excited for. <br /> <br /> <b><u>Changeling</u></b>: Changeling has always drawn on fables and I don't know a fable more foundational to a nation than the legend of King Arthur. Camelot itself can work as a strong analogue for a Freehold and Arthur, the city, and Merlin have been previously mentioned in Changeling's 1e books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T12:48:19-07:00","id":1150737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150735#post1150735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly I want to see that Great War lineage the 2nd edition Promethean core book alluded to <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I got your back on that one, don't worry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T12:59:50-07:00","id":1150743,"title":"","content":"I am amused but also highly confused by Changeling/Mage Wild West. Are we going for magical gunslinger duels?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T13:06:39-07:00","id":1150745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150743#post1150743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am amused but also highly confused by Changeling/Mage Wild West. Are we going for magical gunslinger duels?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean...the feats of guys like Billy the Kid DO sound magical if you think on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T13:07:55-07:00","id":1150746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150743#post1150743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am amused but also highly confused by Changeling/Mage Wild West. Are we going for magical gunslinger duels?</div> </div> </div> </div>The creation of Freeholds is likely the spot of thematic resonance for Changeling. The wild and inhospitable West would be represented by Huntsmen and the Gentry. For Mage, I'm really hoping that its Nameless Orders vs the Seers of the Throne. I'd peg Manifest Destiny as being the primary theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T13:08:49-07:00","id":1150747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150730#post1150730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire has many ties to Arthurian times and as I said in my pitch, the muddled legends and facts of the time are a prime example of how vampires meddle with history.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's interresting, could you elaborate on the ties between Arthurian times and Vampire? Vampires indeed meddle with history but that sounds very unspecific to me. (I mean, you could say the same about any era)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T13:24:50-07:00","id":1150753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150746#post1150746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The creation of Freeholds is likely the spot of thematic resonance for Changeling. The wild and inhospitable West would be represented by Huntsmen and the Gentry. For Mage, I'm really hoping that its Nameless Orders vs the Seers of the Throne. I'd peg Manifest Destiny as being the primary theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Freehold creation and Seer vs Nameless sounds awesome, but now I feel concerned. The horrid consequences Manifest Destiny have often been underplayed and it's so easy to be unintentionally insensitive about native mythology. Hopefully they will avoid connecting Gentry too much to them, and perhaps focus on superstitions and ghost stories?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T13:51:56-07:00","id":1150763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150753#post1150753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Freehold creation and Seer vs Nameless sounds awesome, but now I feel concerned. The horrid consequences Manifest Destiny have often been underplayed and it's so easy to be unintentionally insensitive about native mythology. Hopefully they will avoid connecting Gentry too much to them, and perhaps focus on superstitions and ghost stories?</div> </div> </div> </div>I get where you're coming from. I think all of the Dev team for DE2 has a pretty good track record in that regard, so I'm not too worried.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T13:59:31-07:00","id":1150765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suleri Drals</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150747#post1150747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's interresting, could you elaborate on the ties between Arthurian times and Vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Though you don't just have to repost it there sarcastically, they can just read the reasons themselves. Or not.<br /> <br /> Actual links mostly revolve around the Holy Grail and the Bron bloodline, kings of Britain from this time period, cursed to be without kingdom until they find the Holy Grail. Said Holy Grail has always been a link to immortality (in case you need this in easy mode vampires are immortal), as well as legended as being full of Christ's blood, which probably isn't for everyone but something even the Ordo Dracul has been said to have interest in, not counting the obvious Lance connection. There's even the possibility the Grail legend refers to one of the mythological welsh cauldrons, something that comes up with straight Arthurian legend but that goes with the muddled history part along with the conflicts of Arthur and Bran the Blessed, different versions of what might be the same character.<br /> <br /> As for the themes, you have a land where society is collapsing and its people are constantly under attack. Picts, Scots, Jutes, Saxons, Angles, all preying on the area who lack Roman protection. 'No matter how callous you become, you'll need to move among them.' But how do you keep your Humanity, even if it's a sham, when they're living in these situations? It might fit for a wraith-like nosferatu who feasts on the dying, but the Lords and Serpents strive for more, practically need people, and so need to make a choice to do something in the era. Piety versus Blasphemy should be obvious, even with the West becoming heavily Christian you have them also pointing at neighbors with different practices of the same religion and calling them anathema, and that's before you get to the people who've hearkened back to the 'old ways' (and the older ways) with the retreat of the Romans. Old and New should be obvious, but in case not, this is a point where everything has changed. The Romans were building an Empire, the British were part of it. Now it's gone and all that's left is squabbling, chaotic factions. Remnants of the Empire might try to keep building while enemies might try to eradicate every part, but it's up to the vampires of that time period to deal with what's going on.<br /> <br /> Basically, the time period is the kind of thing that made Vampire Dark Ages popular.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires indeed meddle with history but that sounds very unspecific to me. (I mean, you could say the same about any era) </div> </div> </div>The time period is called 'the darkest of the Dark Ages' due to the lack of historical records. Most of the stories out of the place can be tracked to events that happened elsewhere in different times. That's not even counting the obfuscation of the Romance cycle, and its thematic similarities to Vampire. If you look through the Ventrue and Mekhet clanbooks, though others dip into it, you'll see how this is one method they use to erase things they don't like. For instance what the Mekhet did to Akhenaten. And seeing as how Changeling and Hunter were already picked for the era, I thought Vampire would round them out nicely. I mentioned this during the poll, actually, if you care to look back and read further opinions on it. Though I didn't know which two lines would have been picked at that point, I thought it was going to be Changeling and Mage. The developers said they wanted more of an even spread of gamelines, however, and everyone already picked Mage for Pirates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-18-2017, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T14:01:39-07:00","id":1150766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150753#post1150753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Freehold creation and Seer vs Nameless sounds awesome, but now I feel concerned. The horrid consequences Manifest Destiny have often been underplayed and it's so easy to be unintentionally insensitive about native mythology. Hopefully they will avoid connecting Gentry too much to them, and perhaps focus on superstitions and ghost stories?</div> </div> </div> </div>We already have two Eras that depicted Native Americans and Colonials/Settlers in Doubting Souls and Foreboding Lands. Both that came out relatively well, and depicted both sides well enough to have potential PCs come from either side.<br /> <br /> As such, I feel the devs and OPP can handle this era perfectly fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 10-18-2017, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T14:17:35-07:00","id":1150776,"title":"","content":"I am going to hold back slightly and see how it develops, but thanks for your responses feeling more confident about it now. It definitely has potential to be incredibly fun and memorable!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T15:13:36-07:00","id":1150798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150743#post1150743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am amused but also highly confused by Changeling/Mage Wild West. Are we going for magical gunslinger duels?</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely!<br /> &quot;Your kind took our Arthurian Era! Say your prayers, elf!&quot;<br /> &quot;I reckon it was fair. Your kind took our Pirate Era first. Prepare to die, Merlin!&quot;<br /> Both stare each other down as the tumbleweed blows between them, their hands inches from their revolvers. The sun glares down at the two from above, as each waits for the other to twitch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T15:21:32-07:00","id":1150804,"title":"","content":"Eh, I got Pirate Mage, so maybe it was to much to ask for Arthur Mage and 1001 Nights Mage. After playing Assassin's Creed Unity, the French Revolution era is starting to look more interesting, but I hate to say it, the lack of Arthur Mage has really bummed me out. Not sold on the other eras, but that is how the cookie crumbles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2519-starglyte","name":"Starglyte","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T15:26:42-07:00","id":1150809,"title":"","content":"Apparently Dave Brookshaw has said he would put Mage-Camelot in the Tome of the Pentacle, so I wouldn't get too down about it. I think New York's supposed to be in there as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T16:56:27-07:00","id":1150826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150809#post1150809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently Dave Brookshaw has said he would put Mage-Camelot in the Tome of the Pentacle, so I wouldn't get too down about it. I think New York's supposed to be in there as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooo, where'd that happen?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T17:00:58-07:00","id":1150828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150826#post1150826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oooo, where'd that happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, actually, was just linked to an image with a quote.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/2oGb7nr.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Obviously I can't verify one way or another but I imagine he would confirm or deny it at some point, or the outline would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T17:09:23-07:00","id":1150832,"title":"","content":"I've had a few hours (and beers) to think about it, and I'm okay with the Arthurian Era. I think I'd be disappointed if it *did* happen with Mage without my involvement.<br /> <br /> This way, if we do talk about it in TotP, we'll take the long history Mage has with the myth and run with it without crossover, secure in the knowledge that from a historical perspective, it never happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T17:10:25-07:00","id":1150833,"title":"","content":"We... get pirate mage... instead... of Arthurian Mage...<br /> <br /> I still don't understand why pirates and mages fit together. But sure. Sure...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T17:15:21-07:00","id":1150835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150833#post1150833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We... get pirate mage... instead... of Arthurian Mage...<br /> <br /> I still don't understand why pirates and mages fit together. But sure. Sure...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We're also apparently getting Wild West mage.<br /> <br /> DE2 should be busting at the seems with outlaw mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T17:49:56-07:00","id":1150844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150832#post1150832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've had a few hours (and beers) to think about it, and I'm okay with the Arthurian Era. I think I'd be disappointed if it *did* happen with Mage without my involvement.<br /> <br /> This way, if we do talk about it in TotP, we'll take the long history Mage has with the myth and run with it without crossover, secure in the knowledge that from a historical perspective, it never happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly how I feel. I had toyed with the idea of pitching Arthurian Mage, but it's an era that has been hinted at without being established. I'd rather the writers have more freedom with different gamelines so that the Mage team can build of the lore themselves. <br /> <br /> And that was before I knew about the possibility of Camelot being in Tome of the Pentacle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T18:52:44-07:00","id":1150867,"title":"","content":"Well, about Eras choose to expand I'm... disappointed, mostly. I'm cheered by going with Mage Arthurian times in <b>Tome of Pentacl</b><b>e</b>, but rest...<br /> <br /> I will point the combos I like and those I don't, dwelling a bit on them:<br /> <br /> Pros:<ul><li><span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Great War/Western Front</b> - Geist/ Werewolf/ Promethean - looks great and fitting! The only Era expansion I do not have anything to add, in a good way.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Necropolis of Hawara</b> \u2013 Promethean /Beast /Werewolf - looks unexpected. I like lines combo, only it does not in any way looks for me as 'Necropolis', not going with theme. But I still like looking on 'prehistorical' Promethean, Beast and Werewolf. It's just weird look to see it in this place and time.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Golden Age of Sci Fi</b> - Deviant / Werewolf - Deviant works great, no Promethean, but was sold on Werewolf part earlier to this, so okay.</span></span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Cons:</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>King Arthur\u2019s Britannia</b> \u2013 Hunter/Changeling /Vampire - No Mage is BIG let down. As this part of Era will show up in <b>Tome of Pentacle</b> it's now a bit lower, but I'm still depressed on it. On longer thinking, I may use Vampire for my Vikings Werewolf game ( I already use crossover material with <b>VtR</b> ), but it still seems as really weird choosing. Hunter and Changeling parts I was already all in. But it still hurts we will not see Merlin the Mage in Arthur Times... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Wild West</b> - Changeling/Mage - This is bonkers! We do not have Mage in Arthur, but we got them in Wild West?! We got Nameless War parts in Reconstruction Beast era - Wild West do not seem any how more fitting to it. What will Diamond do in this times? It's 200 years after Europeans entering Americas - it will be mostly everything converted to Diamond, with few Nameless in Native American populations - that's it. Nothing new Mysteries - everything will be stolen to this time, already - nothing very big on social changes. I really do not see any more to do for mages in those time - beside some 'we have lone shamans' of Nameless, Diamond will not have anything to do in it - or worse, we will have very hard stereotyping - Arrows do not have wars to fight as they <i>already</i> are all convertered. If not, we will have literal 'Westerners mage-soldiers are killing our shamans' trope. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Guardians may look from afar on Nameless in Indian populations, but that's it. Mysterium may go to try to join those populations. And Silver Ladder want to bring 'law and order of Atlantis'? I cannot even more concret see Seers activity in here. Compared to Arthurian Britain, it looks as very poor choosing. As to Changeling - I really do not see any parallels. What, we will see towns full of dwarves and elves in the middle of nowhere? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And, what's worse, we DID NOT see Werewolf here - with all the changes in Shadow Realm, all the Native legends and roots of gameline cosmology. No, we got western wizards and elves! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </span></span></span></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-18-2017, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T19:17:40-07:00","id":1150871,"title":"","content":"... you do realize that changeling isn't limited to Norse fairies right? Changeling in the wild west has nothing to do with elves or dwarves....<br /> <br /> I also don't understand why you'd talk about native legends and such as a werewolf thing and not a changeling thing, when changeling is a gameline tied to the legends of the population while werewolf's cosmology doesn't care about the local legends at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T20:39:16-07:00","id":1150885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150867#post1150867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Wild West</b> - Changeling/Mage - This is bonkers! We do not have Mage in Arthur, but we got them in Wild West?! We got Nameless War parts in Reconstruction Beast era - Wild West do not seem any how more fitting to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>...in the Era that wasn't even focused on Mage, and as such only got a couple of paragraphs dedicated to it, and how Reconstruction itself took place during the ending and the aftermath of the Nameless War. If anything, weren't people super frustrated that the Era teased the Nameless War but only referenced it by talking about it's ending and not the war itself?<br /> <br /> If anything, they could use this Era to cover the Nameless War in a lot more depth then what was shown in A Fearful Lesson.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What will Diamond do in this times? It's 200 years after Europeans entering Americas - it will be mostly everything converted to Diamond, with few Nameless in Native American populations - that's it. </div> </div> </div>...not really?<br /> <br /> You make it sound like there's less then a 100 Native Americans around by the time settlers begin to move West. Which is REALLY not true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nothing new Mysteries - everything will be stolen to this time, already - nothing very big on social changes. </div> </div> </div>There's enough pockets of unexplored land to provide a bunch of Mysteries.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, then you're saying a modern-day game of Mage fundamentally can't work because by your logic, all the Mysteries in the US have been solved because the place was conquered by settlers a long time ago.<br /> <br /> Which is obviously not the case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Arrows do not have wars to fight as they <i>already</i> are all convertered. If not, we will have literal 'Westerners mage-soldiers are killing our shamans' trope. </div> </div> </div>Depending on the specific time period, there's that whole Civil War thing going on...and the War of 1812...and the Mexican American War...and the Spanish American War (although this last one I admittedly have doubts on being covered, since this occurs in 1898, aka the end of the 19th century, and technically not occurring in the US itself)...<br /> <br /> Plus looking at Wild West tropes, I can see an Arros masquerading as wandering gun-for-hire or a bounty hunter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Guardians may look from afar on Nameless in Indian populations, but that's it. </div> </div> </div>I dunno, I'd think the Guardians would be in a panic on doing their job.<br /> <br /> Aside from the urban areas, it would be kind of hard for them to do their job if a bunch of mages are scattered throughout lone frontier towns. Not being the wiser that anything happening unless if they actually go to those towns. And who knows if those rumors that had people turning into jackrabbits or the condemned man that survived being hanged are real and the work of a mage, or just the ramblings of the town drunk?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mysterium may go to try to join those populations. </div> </div> </div>...or still head out to the frontiers to seek out new lore and Mysteries. Again, untamed frontiers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And Silver Ladder want to bring 'law and order of Atlantis'? </div> </div> </div>...which does not mean just encroaching on native populations.<br /> <br /> They could be responsible for creating a bunch of said frontier towns. Small places with enough people they could watch over, and personally shepard them to Ascension.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I cannot even more concret see Seers activity in here. </div> </div> </div>Well there are all those Wild West tropes of the tyrannical land/oil/cattle baron that is willing to do anything to achieve profits from the bottom line no matter the human cost. Should be a place to start for any Seers that want to establish a foothold in the West.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Consider this: it's well known that the world of the Wild West depicted in popular media is a VERY inaccurate depiction of the time period. Aside from the flagrant racism from earliest depiction, the high noon duels and the outlaw posses that ravaged lone towns was not as common an occurrence as depicted. If anything, all the townspeople were well armed enough that they could shoot any outlaw gangs out of town.<br /> <br /> So in the world of CofD and in the context of Mage...what if that romanticized view was one great big Lie?<br /> <br /> What if Something happened during the &quot;Wild West&quot; time period that the mages of that time period wanted to cover up? That something happened far more serious then rampant lawlessness and genocide of an indigenous people, that they really don't want Sleepers to remember? That they're content to create a romantic, rosy look on the Wild West and the &quot;good ol' days&quot; that never existed to begin with? Would have happened that they so desperately wanted to hide?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As to Changeling - I really do not see any parallels. What, we will see towns full of dwarves and elves in the middle of nowhere? </div> </div> </div>As already mentioned by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8331_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8331\" data-vbnamecard=\"8331\">milo v3</a> ...no, Changeling is not constrained to Euro-centric mythological figures. Native American myths with their own creatures exist. Hell, its sister game Changeling the Dreaming has a whole race of Native American Changelings in that game. Why can't Changeling the Lost have any?<br /> <br /> If anything, we already have something of a culture clash between changeling settlers and Native settlers. That they're meeting these new people with strange new kiths and not being sure what to make of them.<br /> <br /> And for Changeling's themes as a whole, on changelings trying to establish a new life after escaping their Keepers...perhaps they decided that they needed to physically move away from their former homes and establish a new one with other changelings out in the West. That by moving to a new environment they can truly disconnect themselves from their old life and start a new one.<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Now I'll admit: Mage and Changeling would NOT have been my first choice for Wild West.<br /> <br /> If it was up to me, I would have picked Werewolf and Geist...but since we already have that combo for World War 1, I know that was never going to happen anytime soon.<br /> <br /> However, that's not to say that Mage and Changeling can't fit with the Wild West period. I came up with all the above as the guy who's only read the Mage 2e corebook and who has only read the previews and forum comments on Changeling 2e.<br /> <br /> Besides, if given the choice I would rather the devs come up with weird and atypical choices and pairings to write about over the typical and, frankly, kind of boring choices. Stretches the imagination a bit more with atypical choices, and if done well gives readers something they didn't know they wanted or liked until presented with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 10-18-2017, 11:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T20:42:04-07:00","id":1150886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150765#post1150765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure. Though you don't just have to repost it there sarcastically, they can just read the reasons themselves. Or not.<br /> <br /> Actual links mostly revolve around the Holy Grail and the Bron bloodline, kings of Britain from this time period, cursed to be without kingdom until they find the Holy Grail. Said Holy Grail has always been a link to immortality (in case you need this in easy mode vampires are immortal), as well as legended as being full of Christ's blood, which probably isn't for everyone but something even the Ordo Dracul has been said to have interest in, not counting the obvious Lance connection. There's even the possibility the Grail legend refers to one of the mythological welsh cauldrons, something that comes up with straight Arthurian legend but that goes with the muddled history part along with the conflicts of Arthur and Bran the Blessed, different versions of what might be the same character.<br /> <br /> As for the themes, you have a land where society is collapsing and its people are constantly under attack. Picts, Scots, Jutes, Saxons, Angles, all preying on the area who lack Roman protection. 'No matter how callous you become, you'll need to move among them.' But how do you keep your Humanity, even if it's a sham, when they're living in these situations? It might fit for a wraith-like nosferatu who feasts on the dying, but the Lords and Serpents strive for more, practically need people, and so need to make a choice to do something in the era. Piety versus Blasphemy should be obvious, even with the West becoming heavily Christian you have them also pointing at neighbors with different practices of the same religion and calling them anathema, and that's before you get to the people who've hearkened back to the 'old ways' (and the older ways) with the retreat of the Romans. Old and New should be obvious, but in case not, this is a point where everything has changed. The Romans were building an Empire, the British were part of it. Now it's gone and all that's left is squabbling, chaotic factions. Remnants of the Empire might try to keep building while enemies might try to eradicate every part, but it's up to the vampires of that time period to deal with what's going on.<br /> <br /> Basically, the time period is the kind of thing that made Vampire Dark Ages popular.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The time period is called 'the darkest of the Dark Ages' due to the lack of historical records. Most of the stories out of the place can be tracked to events that happened elsewhere in different times. That's not even counting the obfuscation of the Romance cycle, and its thematic similarities to Vampire. If you look through the Ventrue and Mekhet clanbooks, though others dip into it, you'll see how this is one method they use to erase things they don't like. For instance what the Mekhet did to Akhenaten. And seeing as how Changeling and Hunter were already picked for the era, I thought Vampire would round them out nicely. I mentioned this during the poll, actually, if you care to look back and read further opinions on it. Though I didn't know which two lines would have been picked at that point, I thought it was going to be Changeling and Mage. The developers said they wanted more of an even spread of gamelines, however, and everyone already picked Mage for Pirates.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you for the explanation, it was interesting, I'm pleased with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T20:54:05-07:00","id":1150887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150826#post1150826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oooo, where'd that happen?</div> </div> </div> </div> What did you pick?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T20:55:22-07:00","id":1150888,"title":"","content":"I am quite disappointed at the lack of Geist in Wild West after its mention as an initially gameline exclusive era in Dark Eras 1, seemed ideal to be a Geist &amp; Werewolf/Changeling/Promethean combo setting. Also disappointed a the lack of Promethean in Sci-Fi era, but at least we got Deviant in it. Hopefully the sidebars in the eras will at least mention some interesting stuff for the splats that didn't get the main focus of each setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T21:05:26-07:00","id":1150889,"title":"","content":"I'm really curious as to why Scandinavian Witch Trials, although I can see Mummy &amp; Geist, death. <br /> <br /> Vampires in Camelot was well explained, but Changeling in the Wild West is odd. Just remember Reqiuem for Regina, it would not be good to recon things. <br /> <br /> I couldn't figure out Werewolf in Hawara, although I could see Beast &amp; Promeathan, then I thought Changing Breeds &amp; Egypt. <br /> <br /> Deviant &amp; Sci-Fi is cool. <br /> <br /> I find it ironic that two of my favourite lines ended up in an Era I have little interest in, the Wild West, but maybe it will blow my mind or have cool crossover mechanics. Personally I've never understood the American obsession with the Wild West.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T21:40:26-07:00","id":1150892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150887#post1150887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What did you pick?</div> </div> </div> </div>Promethean to the Great War.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T21:49:51-07:00","id":1150895,"title":"","content":"I thought a lot of choices were surprising, as well. I can easily see Changeling in the Wild West, however, as there were a lot of legends and tall tales about real people and those made up, like Pecos Bill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T21:58:05-07:00","id":1150896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150889#post1150889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really curious as to why Scandinavian Witch Trials, although I can see Mummy &amp; Geist, death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the backer was Swedish, so he wanted an era that covered his home. The Scandinavian version of witchcraft is unique and distinct from the folk magic of the European Plains, which is a plus on that side. After doing some reading, it appears that these witch trials were more focused on stamping out folk magic that people used as medicine and mino mundane boons rather than fear of &quot;black magic.&quot; The suggestion of Mummy was the backer's idea too, since that is a very different location and culture for the Arisen, which I thing was goddamned master stroke. The idea would be that some of the &quot;witches&quot; are actually Sekhem Sorcerers and cultists using Arisen magic for their own benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T22:37:51-07:00","id":1150899,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t have much to say on the actual historical eras, but I am thrilled to see Mummy get the two crossovers I\u2019m most curious about - Demon and Geist - in something finally. I will say that I was quietly hoping for Promethean in Light of the Sun for a long time, as (if it were up to me) Rudolf II\u2019s rule is technically in this period and so the occult and science-obsessed court he had in Prague cries out for it.<br /> <br /> A little sad we aren\u2019t getting Mage in Arthurian Britain, but very happy to see Vampire\u2019s interesting British timeline get more development and the prospect of a more mythical Arthurian Britain for Mage later on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T22:52:43-07:00","id":1150902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150899#post1150899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t have much to say on the actual historical eras, but I am thrilled to see Mummy get the two crossovers I\u2019m most curious about - Demon and Geist - in something finally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded. Mummy/Geist and Mummy Demon are bboth fascinating concepts for crossover to me. I wouldn't be surprised if there was a Krewe or two that decided to sign on as a Mummy's priests. Or foolishly decides that such an abomination of undeath can't be allowed to exist.<br /> <br /> And for Mummy/Demon, it'd be interesting, just because high-level Demons are probably among the few non Arch-Templates beings that could slug it out against the Arisen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T22:58:59-07:00","id":1150903,"title":"","content":"Surprised my one big complaint hasn\u2019t come up yet: I really wanted Promethean for the Golden Age of Sci-Fi, so we could get a 2e update to the Zeka and so we could roll qashmallim into UFO folklore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T23:02:34-07:00","id":1150906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150903#post1150903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Surprised my one big complaint hasn\u2019t come up yet: I really wanted Promethean for the Golden Age of Sci-Fi, so we could get a 2e update to the Zeka and so we could roll qashmallim into UFO folklore.</div> </div> </div> </div>about the Zeka update- isn't that going to be in Night Horrors?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T23:04:45-07:00","id":1150907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150906#post1150906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">about the Zeka update- isn't that going to be in Night Horrors?</div> </div> </div> </div>Was that confirmed? I\u2019m not around here much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T23:50:57-07:00","id":1150915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150907#post1150907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Was that confirmed? I\u2019m not around here much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Matt has noted that it's a &quot;safe assumption&quot; that they'll be in <b>NH: The Tormented</b>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T01:05:55-07:00","id":1150924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150892#post1150892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Promethean to the Great War.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't entirely sure it was you who added it, so let me reiterate my thanks. You're doing the lord (Osiris...) 's work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T08:34:52-07:00","id":1151023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150895#post1150895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought a lot of choices were surprising, as well. I can easily see Changeling in the Wild West, however, as there were a lot of legends and tall tales about real people and those made up, like Pecos Bill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling is all about creating new identities. And how many Westerns are about people seeking revenge for a great slight, or running from the mistakes and tragedies of their past? Plus, literature portrays the Wild West as the romantic Age of the Gunslinger, much like the French <i>\u200bAncien R\u00e9gime </i>is portrayed as the romantic Age of the Swashbuckler: both periods of gallant heroes and beautiful women pursuing their own agendas, both swept aside and replaced by a more mundane era (the decreased lawlessness of the Wild West killed the Gunslinger, the French Revolution killed the Swashbuckler).<br /> <br /> So yeah, I won't be surprised if we see a Changeling Wild West at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T08:41:37-07:00","id":1151025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1151023#post1151023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Changeling is all about creating new identities. And how many Westerns are about people seeking revenge for a great slight, or running from the mistakes and tragedies of their past? Plus, literature portrays the Wild West as the romantic Age of the Gunslinger, much like the French <i>\u200bAncien R\u00e9gime </i>is portrayed as the romantic Age of the Swashbuckler: both periods of gallant heroes and beautiful women pursuing their own agendas, both swept aside and replaced by a more mundane era (the decreased lawlessness of the Wild West killed the Gunslinger, the French Revolution killed the Swashbuckler).<br /> <br /> So yeah, I won't be surprised if we see a Changeling Wild West at some point.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I just got the idea that True Fae would try to abduct people/changelings on moving trains through daring train heists and now I'm stoked for this era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T09:11:56-07:00","id":1151034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150867#post1150867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]<span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Wild West</b> - Changeling/Mage - This is bonkers! We do not have Mage in Arthur, but we got them in Wild West?! We got Nameless War parts in Reconstruction Beast era - Wild West do not seem any how more fitting to it. What will Diamond do in this times? It's 200 years after Europeans entering Americas - it will be mostly everything converted to Diamond, with few Nameless in Native American populations - that's it. Nothing new Mysteries - everything will be stolen to this time, already - nothing very big on social changes. I really do not see any more to do for mages in those time - beside some 'we have lone shamans' of Nameless, Diamond will not have anything to do in it - or worse, we will have very hard stereotyping - Arrows do not have wars to fight as they <i>already</i> are all convertered. If not, we will have literal 'Westerners mage-soldiers are killing our shamans' trope. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Guardians may look from afar on Nameless in Indian populations, but that's it. Mysterium may go to try to join those populations. And Silver Ladder want to bring 'law and order of Atlantis'? I cannot even more concret see Seers activity in here. Compared to Arthurian Britain, it looks as very poor choosing. As to Changeling - I really do not see any parallels. What, we will see towns full of dwarves and elves in the middle of nowhere? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And, what's worse, we DID NOT see Werewolf here - with all the changes in Shadow Realm, all the Native legends and roots of gameline cosmology. No, we got western wizards and elves! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </span></span></span>[/LIST]</div> </div> </div> </div>You are homebrewing the Age of Exploration as a Mage Era, and you can't find even the slightest bit of inspiration or parallels for mages in an era when people are pushing westward to discover and claim new lands? The Western frontier is probably packed with Mysteries, and there's certainly no shortage of cultures clashing. I seriously doubt that they're planning to just make it a game of &quot;Cowboys and Indians&quot; using magic instead of weapons. Personally, I'm intrigued by the possibilities, in no small part because Mage wouldn't have been one I expected for the era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T10:41:43-07:00","id":1151058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1151034#post1151034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are homebrewing the Age of Exploration as a Mage Era, and you can't find even the slightest bit of inspiration or parallels for mages in an era when people are pushing westward to discover and claim new lands? The Western frontier is probably packed with Mysteries, and there's certainly no shortage of cultures clashing. I seriously doubt that they're planning to just make it a game of &quot;Cowboys and Indians&quot; using magic instead of weapons. Personally, I'm intrigued by the possibilities, in no small part because Mage wouldn't have been one I expected for the era.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can easily see Seer Railroad Barons, though. Opposed by the newly formed Free Council that just wants to be left alone on <i>their</i> frontier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T13:16:19-07:00","id":1151099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1151058#post1151058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can easily see Seer Railroad Barons, though. Opposed by the newly formed Free Council that just wants to be left alone on <i>their</i> frontier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not going to lie, I want to see Arrows and Guardians as U.S. Marshals and Texas Rangers now. <br /> <br /> The &quot;cowboys and Indians&quot; angle could be potentially awkward, but it's hardly the sole dimension of Wild West stories. A major one, to be sure, and the writers could (and probably should) devote some page space to discussing that and giving advice on how to handle settler-native interactions. But there's enough stuff besides that to include: train robberies, bank heists, months-long horse chases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T17:18:57-07:00","id":1151160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1151099#post1151099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not going to lie, I want to see Arrows and Guardians as U.S. Marshals and Texas Rangers now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, Guardians of the Veil Pinkertons...ooo, <i>now </i>I'm excited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T18:56:40-07:00","id":1151175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1151160#post1151160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or, Guardians of the Veil Pinkertons...ooo, <i>now </i>I'm excited.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pinkertons are totally seers though, what with all the strike breaking and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T19:41:41-07:00","id":1151189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>World's First Ghost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150733#post1150733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was supposed to be my era suggestion. As happy as I am to have Wild West as a setting, it's a little disheartening to see the focus of it be centered on splats I have no interest in. Neither I nor the other era resurrector had any say in what splats we wanted for our eras, otherwise I'd have pitched something for Geist or Promethean. Wild West was also my second choice, after Mississippi Steamboats, so I'm also a little disappointed that such a unique era in American history doesn't get to be explored.<br /> <br /> But in the end, as long as there are people who get to benefit from my pledge, I can't be too upset. I'm very excited for the other eras, especially the Promethean add-on to the Great War. I'm looking forward to see the final results.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems a strange way to treat a backer if I were in your shoes I'd be pretty annoyed with the result. <br /> Overall I am quite disappointed with the final results. Most of the eras that interest me are connected with gamelines that don't. The original line up is still strong but the additional eras don't excite me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T21:22:28-07:00","id":1151206,"title":"","content":"It should be noted that many of the feats gunslingers achieve in Western fiction can seem pretty damn magical. So fun can be had on recreating those feats for mages:<br /> <br /> -Ridiculously accurate gunshots no matter the range? Apply Forces so that the bullet is directly guided to where it needs to go, or Fate so that the bullets just happen to hit their target almost every time<br /> <br /> -Lighting fast reflexes for quick drawing a revolver? Whip out Time to slow down time so the user has enough of it to draw their gun and line up their shot, or Matter to make the gun just a bit lighter and easier to pull it out of the holster.<br /> <br /> -Surviving a hanging? Use Life to toughen your neck so you don't get choked to death and/or get your neck snapped, or Fate so that the noose just happens to snap at the right time freeing the user.<br /> <br /> Lots of fun stuff like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T22:00:55-07:00","id":1151210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1151175#post1151175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pinkertons are totally seers though, what with all the strike breaking and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>They could well be both. Mundane institutions do get hijacked and not all goals of the Seers are out of line with the Guardians and vice versa. Imagine them being placed on a case togetger and both just have to deal with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T01:51:12-07:00","id":1151241,"title":"","content":"My problem with the Mummies in renaissance Scandinavia is... Well.. What would Mummies be doing up here then? The contacts between the north and Africa has generally been minimal, and there's 0 reason for a Mummy to be up here.<br /> I suppose a cult or two could have found their way here, but here, more than any other game with Mummy, it becomes extremely contrived to play more than 1 Mummy. They are rare enough to begin with, and this is a place that shouldn't have them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T01:58:32-07:00","id":1151244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1151241#post1151241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem with the Mummies in renaissance Scandinavia is... Well.. What would Mummies be doing up here then? The contacts between the north and Africa has generally been minimal, and there's 0 reason for a Mummy to be up here.<br /> I suppose a cult or two could have found their way here, but here, more than any other game with Mummy, it becomes extremely contrived to play more than 1 Mummy. They are rare enough to begin with, and this is a place that shouldn't have them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's my general problem with <b>Mummy: The Curse</b> as gameline - HOW 'Egypt area only' mummies are found around world? But I think it's problem to general Mummy's forum, so this will go there, in new topic I do.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T04:29:24-07:00","id":1151264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1151241#post1151241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem with the Mummies in renaissance Scandinavia is... Well.. What would Mummies be doing up here then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunting for relics which appear pretty much everywhere. Maybe there's something specifically there that's of interest to the Arisen. Maybe an Arisen has decided to run their own project there.<br /> <br /> There are any number of potential reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The contacts between the north and Africa has generally been minimal, and there's 0 reason for a Mummy to be up here. </div> </div> </div>Most Arisen left Egypt over 4000 years ago. They don't need to have migrated straight there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I suppose a cult or two could have found their way here, but here, more than any other game with Mummy, it becomes extremely contrived to play more than 1 Mummy. They are rare enough to begin with, and this is a place that shouldn't have them. </div> </div> </div>If a modern city can have twenty Arisen, a whole region can probably have the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T05:50:14-07:00","id":1151284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1151264#post1151264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hunting for relics which appear pretty much everywhere. Maybe there's something specifically there that's of interest to the Arisen. Maybe an Arisen has decided to run their own project there.<br /> <br /> There are any number of potential reasons.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Most Arisen left Egypt over 4000 years ago. They don't need to have migrated straight there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If a modern city can have twenty Arisen, a whole region can probably have the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scandinavia has always been really scarcely populated. It is even today. The entire nation of Sweden has about the same population of the Chicago Metro Area. So modern Sweden ought to have some 20 Mummies.<br /> The North doesn't really have any major pull. Vampires, Werewolves, Mages, Changelings and Geister all make sense, since they don't have to get up here - they are born here. Mummies have to travel. It's really only good as a hiding place. And as I said, more than one Mummy in a game will require a lot of suspension of disbelief.<br /> <br /> Literally anywhere else in Europe would be a better place to look for Relics during this time, since they will be a lot more highly populated, more densely populated, and have a longer history. Relics will be rarer, and it will be a lot longer between them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T09:26:38-07:00","id":1151357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1151284#post1151284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scandinavia has always been really scarcely populated. It is even today. The entire nation of Sweden has about the same population of the Chicago Metro Area. So modern Sweden ought to have some 20 Mummies.</div> </div> </div> </div>So? Mummies don't need a big population.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The North doesn't really have any major pull. </div> </div> </div>The era covers the height of the Swedish Empire; lots of Arisen like political influence and power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires, Werewolves, Mages, Changelings and Geister all make sense, since they don't have to get up here - they are born here. Mummies have to travel. </div> </div> </div>Which they have thousands of years to do. They've gone everywhere else, but Scandinavia is a step too far.<br /> <br /> Also, unless all the clans originated in Scandinavia, then vampires did have to travel there at some point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Literally anywhere else in Europe would be a better place to look for Relics during this time, since they will be a lot more highly populated, more densely populated, and have a longer history. Relics will be rarer, and it will be a lot longer between them. </div> </div> </div>Unless there's some kind of special reason for there to be more relics than might be expected. That's the kind of special case that we can reasonably expect from a Dark Era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T09:33:29-07:00","id":1151362,"title":"","content":"Can you tell me,if one of backers allowed to add splats to eras had suggested Inferno,would Inferno have been added? I really wante to suggest it for the seven wonders but i didnt had the money","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T09:41:36-07:00","id":1151364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1151362#post1151362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you tell me,if one of backers allowed to add splats to eras had suggested Inferno,would Inferno have been added? I really wante to suggest it for the seven wonders but i didnt had the money</div> </div> </div> </div>We did ask about minor splats and blue book, but the Devs requested we stick to main gamelines. So no, Inferno would have been a no-go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T13:10:24-07:00","id":1151437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1151244#post1151244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's my general problem with <b>Mummy: The Curse</b> as gameline - HOW 'Egypt area only' mummies are found around world? But I think it's problem to general Mummy's forum, so this will go there, in new topic I do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it would be an untrue statement about the game line? Long story short, after their first awakening the Arisen en mass dispersed from their original lands to far flung parts of the globe. Also the game line leaves open mummies who found themselves interred in outposts of the Empire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 10-20-2017, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T13:20:06-07:00","id":1151439,"title":"","content":"Sigh, so bummed at no werewolf-knights... damned confused that they ended up in Egypt but to each their prey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T13:33:31-07:00","id":1151446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1151439#post1151439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sigh, so bummed at no werewolf-knights... damned confused that they ended up in Egypt but to each their prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was said once or twice that any case of Werewolf and Egypt could end up involving <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wepwawet\" target=\"_blank\">Wepwawet</a> in once form or another, but I don't remember who said it and where, or if the claim would still be valid for this Era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T13:41:14-07:00","id":1151454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1151446#post1151446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it was said once or twice that any case of Werewolf and Egypt could end up involving <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wepwawet\" target=\"_blank\">Wepwawet</a> in once form or another, but I don't remember who said it and where, or if the claim would still be valid for this Era.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was explicitly mentioned in the elevator pitch for adding Werewolves to this era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T13:45:45-07:00","id":1151456,"title":"","content":"My other pitch was for Qing era werewolves. With a focus on the Pure being in power as drivers behind the Qing (Pure) Dynasty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T08:21:58-07:00","id":1152809,"title":"","content":"Considering that The Arisen have setting books for Washington DC and Rio De Janeiro, that the Scandinavian lands have had trade relations with the middle east and african nations for centuries.((there has been found a lot of coins from the caliphate in visby for example)) And that the Arisen have been extensively traveling for millenia, i don't see why they can't be in Scandinavia. Especially if something sufficiently interesting is occurring there to draw their attention to the place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T12:20:42-07:00","id":1152872,"title":"","content":"consider also that there is a significantly larger distance between Egypt and China as compared to Egypt and Scandinavia, and i am pretty sure it becomes less unrealistic. I don't see any outcry against the last imperials for starters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T12:28:32-07:00","id":1152873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1152872#post1152872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">consider also that there is a significantly larger distance between Egypt and China as compared to Egypt and Scandinavia, and i am pretty sure it becomes less unrealistic. I don't see any outcry against the last imperials for starters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or Rio for that matter, where Mummies have been since long before this era, and which is almost twice as far away as Scandinavia, AND which has no land route to connect them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T07:12:23-07:00","id":1153160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1152872#post1152872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">consider also that there is a significantly larger distance between Egypt and China as compared to Egypt and Scandinavia, and i am pretty sure it becomes less unrealistic. I don't see any outcry against the last imperials for starters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because there have long been trade routes to India, from the middle east, as well as from China. Travel there is fairly reasonable.<br /> But yeah, I agree with Rio as well. It's a stupid place.<br /> Mummies fit in places with lots of history of civilization, and a reasonable assumption that one could get there from the near- and middle east.<br /> So, The Middle East, African East Coast, all around the Mediterranean, Persia, India, Indochina, and China. And due to the rationalization of Infrastructure portals, Mesoamerica. Beyond that, it feels way too contrived.<br /> No real reason to be in the place, and no reasonable way to get there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T08:46:17-07:00","id":1153186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1153160#post1153160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because there have long been trade routes to India, from the middle east, as well as from China. Travel there is fairly reasonable.<br /> But yeah, I agree with Rio as well. It's a stupid place.<br /> Mummies fit in places with lots of history of civilization, and a reasonable assumption that one could get there from the near- and middle east.<br /> So, The Middle East, African East Coast, all around the Mediterranean, Persia, India, Indochina, and China. And due to the rationalization of Infrastructure portals, Mesoamerica. Beyond that, it feels way too contrived.<br /> No real reason to be in the place, and no reasonable way to get there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good thing that Scandinavia was never known for its extensive trade routes, and those Viking blokes had no interaction with the outside world. Gosh, imagine how silly we\u2019d feel if they\u2019d made it as far as Byzantium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12958-raz_fox","name":"Raz_Fox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T09:00:13-07:00","id":1153189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1153160#post1153160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and no reasonable way to get there.</div> </div> </div> </div>They mostly went by boat. There are a few pre-columbian mummies who got there by weird event, but most just got on a ship after the Portuguese conquest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T09:46:47-07:00","id":1153206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1153160#post1153160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because there have long been trade routes to India, from the middle east, as well as from China. Travel there is fairly reasonable.<br /> But yeah, I agree with Rio as well. It's a stupid place.<br /> Mummies fit in places with lots of history of civilization, and a reasonable assumption that one could get there from the near- and middle east.<br /> So, The Middle East, African East Coast, all around the Mediterranean, Persia, India, Indochina, and China. And due to the rationalization of Infrastructure portals, Mesoamerica. Beyond that, it feels way too contrived.<br /> No real reason to be in the place, and no reasonable way to get there.</div> </div> </div> </div>So genuine question that is not meant to be snarky or sarcastic. Have you read Cursed Necropolis: Rio? Because actually does seem to be a really damn good reason for Mummies to be there.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">There's Relic architecture that predates the Rite of Return by thousands of years buried beneath the city. And it really messes with a Mummy's memories and power levels.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That is more than enough impetus for Fate or the Judges to send Mummies to South America. And I really do think that saying there is no reasonable way for Mummies to make it across the Atlantic when the Arisen are sacred walking corpses with biblical superpowers capable of nudging fate so that asteroids fall on top of their enemies is over the top in terms of expectations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T10:38:28-07:00","id":1153221,"title":"","content":"Like, there's literally a power that let's them open a portal and go wherever Fate thinks they ought to end up, the Shan'iatu literally set up way points to let them go anywhere in the world, we're talking about people from a civilization that pushed technological advancements like whoa, and that's before you account for them working with and manipulating other splats and powers to their own ends.<br /> <br /> When the world is made on the principles you laid down, you find ways to travel the whole of it sooner or later, regardless of how large it is. Destination is a state of mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T16:44:23-07:00","id":1154881,"title":"","content":"So I just found <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Soulstealers-Chinese-Sorcery-Scare-1768/dp/0674821513\" target=\"_blank\">this little gem</a>. Now I'm really hoping 1768 is the focus year for Last Imperials, because I don't think I've ever seen something that is more Mummy and Hunter at the same time than this sorcery scare. It got pretty solid academic reviews too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T00:35:44-08:00","id":1158796,"title":"","content":"I am unsure if anyone remembers but earlier in the thread, I did mention that I was working on my own little homebrew for a Steamboat Era setting for Changeling the Lost. <br /> <br /> I had hoped to have it completed well before now but unfortunately, life got in the way somewhat. Anyway, it is coming out of editing at the moment and as it does, I am uploading it on a WoD play by post site that I contribute to. <br /> <br /> If anyone is interested in taking a look, I will post a link.<br /> <br /> It seems an appropriate day to bring this up considering the Changeling 2e Kickstarter was launched today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11747-wh157l3r","name":"wh157l3r","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T03:58:22-08:00","id":1158862,"title":"","content":"I'd be curious to see it, particularly since steamboats didn't make the final book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T12:50:46-08:00","id":1159128,"title":"","content":"In that case I will post a link when I get home from work.<br /> <br /> At the moment it is mostly background historical information and some optional rules around the Resource Merit which aims to reinforce the high risk, high reward nature of the Era.<br /> <br /> The total write up tops out at about 20,000 words. I may have gone a bit too far into the historical information regarding the setting but since it adds so much flavor I couldn't help myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11747-wh157l3r","name":"wh157l3r","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T12:58:52-08:00","id":1159133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wh157l3r</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1159128#post1159128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the moment it is mostly background historical information and some optional rules around the Resource Merit which aims to reinforce the high risk, high reward nature of the Era.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there are Steamboats, there should be cash and gamble. I remember someone pointed that <i>Chase</i> rules from <b>CoD Rulebook </b>could be used for gamble and card games simulations. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T17:00:13-08:00","id":1159255,"title":"","content":"I will have to look into that. <br /> <br /> My optional rules revovle around how Reaources can be invested and either won or lost at a party level at the moment.<br /> <br /> Its rough but it should result in player being much more invested when their vessel runs up a sandbank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11747-wh157l3r","name":"wh157l3r","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T09:06:31-08:00","id":1165883,"title":"","content":"Soooo... It looks like <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/DarkerDaysRadio/posts/10154814913091076\" target=\"_blank\">Darker Days Radio is interviewing Meghan</a> on Saturday. If you've got questions to ask about Dark Eras 2, go post them on DDR's facebook!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T12:26:37-08:00","id":1165911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1150730#post1150730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The three-gameline eras are due to backers. Vampires in Arthurian time are from me, for instance. Previously it was Changeling and Hunter. Vampire has many ties to Arthurian times and as I said in my pitch, the muddled legends and facts of the time are a prime example of how vampires meddle with history.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I could, in fact, kiss you for that. <br /> <br /> Platonically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T21:20:12-08:00","id":1166602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1166553#post1166553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://podcast.darker-days.org/e/83-hedge-funding/\" target=\"_blank\">And said podcast is now up.</a><br /> <br /> Also includes some questions regarding Dark Eras 2 and the recently released Half-Damned for VtR2.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1166589#post1166589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting to learn Meghan is doing the Golden Age of Piracy (Mage/Geist), French Revolution (Demon/Mage/Mummy), Necropolis of Harawa (Werewolf/Promethean/Beast), Wild West (Mage/Changeling), and 1,001 Nights eras (Beast/Vampire). Of those only Wild West is for Changeling 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't make my hopes high they fixed the worst gameline Dark Eras choosing for French Revolution, ever, with correct one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> We will never get true Nameless War setting for Mage... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T21:26:27-08:00","id":1166605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1166602#post1166602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Don't make my hopes high they fixed the worst gameline Dark Eras choosing for French Revolution, ever, with correct one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> We will never get true Nameless War setting for Mage... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Was this really necessary to post in both this and the Changeling Kicckstarter thread? Give it up man. Being this bitter about the lines chosen for DE2 can't be healthy and it's not going to change anything. It just starts bitter fights that make the forums toxic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T23:56:58-08:00","id":1166644,"title":"","content":"I will just point Brandford answer to this subtopic in Changeling topic, with which I agree on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1166617#post1166617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe Dave said DE2 wasn't the place to discuss the Nameless War, but rather<i> if</i> Mage wasn't included in the relevant era, it would be included in Tome of the Pentacle. Since Dave surprisingly doesn't seem to be writing or developing anything for DE2, I personally prefer he develop or write on the subject in TofP. I can nevertheless see why some are disappointed by certain choices for DE2.<br /> <br /> Regardless, the above has nothing to do with Meghan's development or writing skills or the content of Changeling 2e, and it would be patently absurd to judge Changeling or Meghan by OPP's splat and era choices in DE2.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T01:13:06-08:00","id":1166653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1166644#post1166644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will just point Brandford answer to this subtopic in Changeling topic, with which I agree on.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And now you're just needlessly deflecting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T01:32:08-08:00","id":1166658,"title":"","content":"<b>Well, if I'm to be honest - I only weep on no Mage: the Awakening in French Revolution.</b> What gamelines for it will be in DE2 will be are little interest for me, really. What I can say I can understand <b>Vampire: the Requiem</b> - VtR has some strong 'revolution vamps' leftovers from VtM and canonical event for creation of Carthian Movement. Even if I do not personally agree with whole idea 'if it has revolution, it need to have <b>Demon: The Descent</b>', but can see this angle build in gameline with rebeling on God Machine so central to game. BUT I really do not see how Mummy: The Curse is better game to have in French Revolution Era where in MtAw you have <i>literal</i> start of Nameless War, i.e. starting point of Free Council creation and modern Seers of Throne rebuild. It's like creation/remake of 2 of 6 main factions in gameline! IF Mage would be in choices, Mummy would not sting me a bit.<br /> <br /> Don't worry, I have similar problem with no Arthurian Mage in DE2, but on much lesser scale. Or that we will get Mage and Changeling Wild West that is... strange. <i>Really</i> strange.<br /> <br /> French Revolution Era gameline choices are most hurting me because how important it's to Mage games lore. It's, in some way. as important as <i>Sundered World</i> is for <b>WerewolfL The Forsaken</b>. Rest of choosing are more 'oh, well, some gamelines do not jive, but I will live with no canon info on those'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-11-2017, 04:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T09:11:17-08:00","id":1166724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1166617#post1166617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless, the above has nothing to do with Meghan's development or writing skills or the content of Changeling 2e, and it would be patently absurd to judge Changeling or Meghan by OPP's splat and era choices in DE2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet I would argue that suggesting the selection of these gamelines for this era is the &quot;worst choice&quot; is a slam on Meghan's choices. She is one of the Developers of this book.She was assumably part of the decision-making process that led to assigning Vampire and Demon, and not Mage, to French Revolution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1166658#post1166658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Well, if I'm to be honest - I only weep on no Mage: the Awakening in French Revolution.</b> What gamelines for it will be in DE2 will be are little interest for me, really. [...] IF Mage would be in choices, Mummy would not sting me a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's how this reads to me: &quot;I'm okay if everyone gets to have neat things, as long as the things I think are fun get first priority.&quot; I'm certain that's not what you are literally thinking, but this is how you are projecting yourself. And frankly, its rude. We all have things we wanted in DE2 we didn't get. I wanted Changeling Hawara. I wanted Mummy Golden Age of Sci-Fi. I wanted Hunter Pirates. I wanted Mage 1001 Nights. I wanted Promethean Arthur. I wanted Geist Hawara. I wanted Gilgamesh to get revived as an era. You get the picture. Most of us have moved on from wanting something we didn't get because there is no point in being angry and dwelling in the past, especially when there is so much other stuff to be excited about. At this point, you probably need to do the same.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1166658#post1166658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BUT I really do not see how Mummy: The Curse is better game to have in French Revolution Era where in MtAw you have <i>literal</i> start of Nameless War, i.e. starting point of Free Council creation and modern Seers of Throne rebuild.</div> </div> </div> </div><u><b>Point 1</b></u><br /> I agree with you, Mage is a pretty much perfect fit for this era. But you know what I think is an even better fit? Mummy. You refuse to read Mummy, which is fine, but that means you don't know what themes the game has developed. That makes it pretty impossible for you to say &quot;but this gameline is a better fit thematicly&quot; because you are trying to compare something you know very well to something you haven't researched.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Point 2</b></u><br /> You are trying to make this arguement objective. It's not. It's subjective, based on the tastes of the individuals involved, which is why I keep saying its okay if you don't like the choices that have been made. That, however, undercuts your ability to argue that &quot;this is clearly a bad decision&quot; because people are allowed to disagree with your premise since again, this is a subjective matter of taste.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Point 3</b></u><br /> Mummy to French Revolution was on my short list of addons I would have liked to do. I didn't end up going that route, but I am overwhelming happy that someone else did. Every time you bring up something like &quot;why would anyone choose Mummy&quot; or &quot;Mage is a superior choice&quot; or &quot;this idea is the worst&quot; it feels like a personal attack on me and my preferences. Is it meant to? Probably not, but it sure as hell feels like it. It makes me not want to participate in this forums anymore and that is not cool. Following on with that logic...<br /> <br /> <u><b>Point 4</b></u><br /> The person who added Mummy to French hasn't come forth to my knowledge, but they are a member of this community. In fact, I would add the words &quot;well-respected&quot; to the front of that statement. Saying that Mummy was the &quot;worst gameline choice ever&quot; to add to French Revolution absolutely is a personal attack on their decisions. Saying you disagree with their choice is one thing, constantly attacking their decision every time it gets brought up is rude, toxic, and hostile. If I feel like I don't want to participate on the forums anymore because of what you keep saying, how do you think they, who actually did add that era to the book, feel?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1166658#post1166658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't worry, I have similar problem with no Arthurian Mage in DE2, but on much lesser scale .</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't make what you've said any better or less judgemental.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1166658#post1166658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">French Revolution Era gameline choices are most hurting me because how important it's to Mage games lore. It's, in some way. as important as <i>Sundered World</i> is for <b>WerewolfL The Forsaken</b>. Rest of choosing are more 'oh, well, some gamelines do not jive, but I will live with no canon info on those'.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, funny thing. Werewolf was a playable game before Sundered World came along. Werewolf is a playable game if you ignore Sundered World. Did Sundered World create new opportunities for Werewolf games? Totally. Is so important as to be absolutely essential that you have it for any Werewolf game? Not a chance. By the same token, having French Revolution Mage would be very nice, but no matter how important an era it is for Mage's history, it's not an indispensable time period that must be explored in order for the setting to make sense. Its loss is ultimately minor in the big picture.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Tl;dr</b></u>: You're taking this too far and making a mountain out of a molehill. We've discussed this topic before and as far as I can tell, you've ignored the advice people have given you on this topic. Now it is making me (and probably others too) not want to discuss a book I spend hundreds of dollars backing and am super excited for. For everyone's sake, please let it go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 12-11-2017, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T09:36:33-08:00","id":1166730,"title":"","content":"The French Revolution is in no way as important to Mage's setting as the Sundering (which, you must note, the Sundered World doesn't even <i>depict</i>) is to Werewolf's. That's just... Ridiculous hyperbole.<br /> <br /> None of the Mage eras in DE2 are &quot;important&quot; the way To The Strongest was in DE1. And that's fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T11:53:26-08:00","id":1166757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1166658#post1166658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Well, if I'm to be honest - I only weep on no Mage: the Awakening in French Revolution.</b> What gamelines for it will be in DE2 will be are little interest for me, really. What I can say I can understand <b>Vampire: the Requiem</b> - VtR has some strong 'revolution vamps' leftovers from VtM and canonical event for creation of Carthian Movement. Even if I do not personally agree with whole idea 'if it has revolution, it need to have <b>Demon: The Descent</b>', but can see this angle build in gameline with rebeling on God Machine so central to game. BUT I really do not see how Mummy: The Curse is better game to have in French Revolution Era where in MtAw you have <i>literal</i> start of Nameless War, i.e. starting point of Free Council creation and modern Seers of Throne rebuild. It's like creation/remake of 2 of 6 main factions in gameline! IF Mage would be in choices, Mummy would not sting me a bit.<br /> <br /> Don't worry, I have similar problem with no Arthurian Mage in DE2, but on much lesser scale. Or that we will get Mage and Changeling Wild West that is... strange. <i>Really</i> strange.<br /> <br /> French Revolution Era gameline choices are most hurting me because how important it's to Mage games lore. It's, in some way. as important as <i>Sundered World</i> is for <b>WerewolfL The Forsaken</b>. Rest of choosing are more 'oh, well, some gamelines do not jive, but I will live with no canon info on those'.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all but impossible to give you any benefit of the doubt when, if memory serves as it might have been a different thread, you intentionally mis-characterized Mummy and then later admitted you haven't even read the material. While I am mildly biased in that Mummy is my favourite ChroD game at the moment...well Mage is my second.My guess is that, beyond Brookshaw's helpful commentary on the relative importance of eras, any good pitch person would been able to pitch to a developer what particular themes from an era play well with any particular game line. There's a fine line between being an advocate or having a love of something and becoming a homer for it to the detriment of the fans of other things. That's a dis-service to yourself and to fans of other material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 12-11-2017, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T13:05:29-08:00","id":1166777,"title":"","content":"Hamster, I want to join my voice with those here and just say that I am disappointed that this is the way you are treating the matter. Problems you may have, but I've come to think of you as that guy who does handle what other people like with some care, and I quite like holding you up as someone who people can disagree with and still get along with, no real hurt being caused. This is not a good display of that trait I admired.<br /> <br /> You're better than this, man. I know you are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T21:21:02-08:00","id":1166905,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Wyrdhamster, let it go. Don't bring up the subject again, thank you.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T02:49:43-08:00","id":1166939,"title":"","content":"Do people really not understand Mummy and the French Revolution? Besides the obvious theme of the laboring class revolting against tyrannical overlords there's the fact that it's the only occidental Dark Era <i>for</i> Mummy.<br /> <br /> We have ancient Egypt, medieval sub-Saharan Africa, and China. You can argue Ruins of Empire but it's split between Egypt, Turkey, and Britain, with French territories only added from backer expansion. French Revolution, as trite as maybe some people think a European Dark Era is, is Mummy's first Era of such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T03:57:40-08:00","id":1166945,"title":"","content":"People, I haven't checked this thread since the Kickstarter, but I'll be blunt and say that while not all Dark Eras align with a gameline I expected, I 100% am sure that what we'll get will be interesting to have.<br /> <br /> Besides, we all know that sometimes going for a curve ball is better and it's not like the Era that's causing trouble does not fit. It's a cool suggestion made by someone that the writers will take seriously while working on it.<br /> <br /> It might not what you wanted the most (each one of us has a dream Era that did not happen), but that's not an excuse to treat It that way. I lobbied for some Eras during the Kickstarter myself but it was all good-natured: we'll still get good stuff anyways.<br /> <br /> We're getting past what's passionate into &quot;dude, not cool&quot; realm here","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T12:38:14-08:00","id":1167083,"title":"","content":"Changing topics back to the podcast, Meghan also said that the era she's most excited for is Pirates, so I am very interested in seeing how that one pans out above and beyond my preexisting anticipation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"fo