mere as a Diamond Order.<br /> <br /> PS: I think we'd know more once Nameless and Accursed gets published, with perhaps some more historical info in Tome of the Pentacle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":216,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","user":"Zooroos","date":".  Afditional info 08-09-2019, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T00:42:02-07:00","id":1330218,"title":"","content":"I think in general Dave said he wouldn't be entirely comfortable having something as major as the Tremere be in DE2, aka a book he isn't directly developing for, and would rather have their 2e write-up in a Mage2e book.<br /> <br /> (see why he was ultimately glad the Britania era wasn't selected to be a Mage Era)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 08-10-2019, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T10:45:30-07:00","id":1330776,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Tremere already weren't a Diamond Order by the time any of the Mage eras happen. It's mentioned briefly in one or two of the &quot;what are the other game lines up to?&quot; sidebars, though. Their full 2e write-up is in Nameless &amp; Accursed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b