by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1361263#post1361263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Bloodless are still in there. they are in the French Revolution chapter. its when a vampire decides to feed vitae to a sleeping mummy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> it isn't statted they just mentioned it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T04:48:14-08:00","id":1361435,"title":"","content":"So two things I must note as I go through the book-<br /> <br /> 1) An angel called Zain? Really? Really?...<br /> <br /> 2) the Eater of Names is coming to end us all!<br /> <br /> 3) Bird is on the loose! I repeat, Bird is on the loose! Don't look it in the Eye! I repeat, DON&quot;T LOOK IT IN THE EYE! THE EYE IS ALIVE! THE EYE IS ALIVE!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 01-17-2020, 07:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T05:33:08-08:00","id":1361441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1361435#post1361435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So two things I must note as I go through the book-<br /> <br /> 1) An angel called Zain? Really? Really?...</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there something wrong with that name? I plucked it from a list of potential names I was provided during my second draft, but I didn\u2019t research it further, so if it\u2019s problematic, that\u2019s on me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T05:40:30-08:00","id":1361443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1361441#post1361441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is there something wrong with that name? I plucked it from a list of potential names I was provided during my second draft, but I didn\u2019t research it further, so if it\u2019s problematic, that\u2019s on me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like, not <i>problematic</i>, just kind of thing that modern Hebrew native speakers would find funny.<br /> <br /> Like, sure Zain is the seventh letter in the hebrew alphabet. It is also the archaic name for a weapon, which makes a lot of sense for an angel. Due to that connotation to a weapon, it is also used in modern hebrew as a slang word for male genitalia. <br /> <br /> I mean, again, in the said Era it makes sense, and its meaning as a weapon fits an angel- but the slang term is so deeply rooted in modern hebrew that native speakers probably can't not say &quot;really?&quot; when they look at it :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T07:21:37-08:00","id":1361456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1361443#post1361443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, not <i>problematic</i>, just kind of thing that modern Hebrew native speakers would find funny.<br /> <br /> Like, sure Zain is the seventh letter in the hebrew alphabet. It is also the archaic name for a weapon, which makes a lot of sense for an angel. Due to that connotation to a weapon, it is also used in modern hebrew as a slang word for male genitalia. <br /> <br /> I mean, again, in the said Era it makes sense, and its meaning as a weapon fits an angel- but the slang term is so deeply rooted in modern hebrew that native speakers probably can't not say &amp;quot;really?&amp;quot; when they look at it :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, okay. Thank you for telling me. I was worried I\u2019d been offensive with it. Unintentionally hilarious is something I can deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T15:27:34-08:00","id":1361582,"title":"","content":"That ancient Kemet Era with Werewolves involved in Death Wolf's war with his own rank 7 shade over the remains of a rotting Pangean is amazing. Just cannot get over how absolutely metal that whole section was. <br /> <br /> As a Mage fan, the Golden Age of Piracy section was everything I wanted. Just oozing with disturbing Mysteries and some of the best Order-related plot hooks in any Mage book. The Geist stuff just fit in so well, with Maroons practicing Obeah and Davy Jones as a Reaper. Loved all of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T16:27:06-08:00","id":1361602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1361582#post1361582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That ancient Kemet Era with Werewolves involved in Death Wolf's war with his own rank 7 shade over the remains of a rotting Pangean is amazing. Just cannot get over how absolutely metal that whole section was.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's more in WW1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T21:04:44-08:00","id":1361652,"title":"","content":"If I had known about the werecrocs I would have backed this. Now I have to regret it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T21:09:26-08:00","id":1361654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryphon's Feather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1361652#post1361652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I had known about the werecrocs I would have backed this. Now I have to regret it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s still time to preorder it through the KS page\u2019s link to backerkit, if that\u2019s something you are interested in doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T14:46:32-08:00","id":1362240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ForgeEternal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1361186#post1361186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2229_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2229\" data-vbnamecard=\"2229\">Meghan Fitzgerald</a> Thanks for the quick answer! Any chance of seeing the remaining attainments in another book at some point?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible! I can make no promises but I would like to explore options to get more full Legacies written up somewhere, sometime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T05:24:29-08:00","id":1365984,"title":"","content":"Hey <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> , Good job with Thousand and One Nightmares, but I have a big question for you:<br /> <br /> Why no Nasir al-Din Tusi? Like, I get the splat choice has it's limits, the Thousand and One Nights needs to be a major played theme, and the sheer amount of scientific and mathematic advancements in the Islamic golden age is A LOT, but still, No direct mention of my man Tusi? That's a missed opportunity right there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-07-2020, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T05:54:19-08:00","id":1365992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1365984#post1365984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> , Good job with Thousand and One Nightmares, but I have a big question for you:<br /> <br /> Why no Nasir al-Din Tusi? Like, I get the splat choice has it's limits, the Thousand and One Nights needs to be a major played theme, and the sheer amount of scientific and mathematic advancements in the Islamic golden age is A LOT, but still, No direct mention of my man Tusi? That's a missed opportunity right there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Timeframe. Only place he would have fit was the timeline because everything else\u2019s was tightly focused on 832, a solid four centuries before he was alive. And I had to trim that timeline several times to keep it reasonable. If/when I get a chance to flesh out the Nizari State and/or the Mongol invasions, he\u2019ll get some mentions.","signature":"<hr