eelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T12:44:03-07:00","id":1376985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1100689-dark-eras-2-discussion-thread?p=1376980#post1376980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As one of the writers on the era, I'd love to see the elaboration! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I' half way through the French Revolution, so we'll have to see how it holds out against that and the remaining three, but so far it's definitely in my top four of Dark Eras 2, and when I have that cemented down, I'm definitely gonna give a breakdown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T09:54:48-07:00","id":1377360,"title":"","content":"The Tenth Choir did nothing wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T15:56:45-07:00","id":1377402,"title":"","content":"So, before Mysterious Frontiers commentary:<br /> <br /> I think it would be inappropriate to describe Dark Eras and Dark Eras Companion as uneven in comparison to Dark Eras 2-honestly, the entire project born from that Kickstarter has a lot of eras that are really fun, well researched, and well designed, and that if there is a feeling of unevenness, it has more to do with with the mass of Eras that allows for more chance for stand-outs and plunkers to happen. That said, Dark Eras 2 is remarkably consistent in terms of it's quality, and I don't think it's surprising that when the discussion of favorites came up, it was much more wildly bent to taste. What I'm saying is that this book is sgood and clearly learned from the lessons of DE1.<br /> <br /> So, that said, two points regarding Mysterious Frontiers:<br /> <br /> 1) That's cheating.<br /> <br /> 2) So the Yukon Gold Rush obviously is not a focus, but it's just close enough that it reinforces for me, as someone who read The Life and Times of Scrooge McDuck, that someone needs to play him as a Mysterium mage.<br /> <br /> That said, I've got a madam-&quot;mayor&quot; of a magic-supported town to design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T23:50:33-07:00","id":1382458,"title":"","content":"Still chewing my way through DE2 slowly but surely. Hasn't helped that I've been trying to get to other books that have piled up on my backlog. I've also been jumping around a bit in terms of Eras to read, prioritizing the ones I have the most interest in. So far I've finished reading &quot;The Devil and the Deep Blue Sea&quot;, &quot;Reign of Terror&quot;, &quot;Mysterious Frontiers&quot;, &quot;The Great War&quot; and &quot;Fear and the Golden Promise of Tomorrow&quot;.<br /> <br /> Currently on &quot;Arthur's Britannia&quot;...and something interesting I noticed. The Uratha get mentioned a lot throughout the Era's write-up. Mentions beyond its section in sidebar explaining what the other non-focus splats were doing, and despite the era being a Vampire/Changeling/Hunter Era. So...<br /> <br /> -Was the Era originally conceived to include Werewolf and the mentions are an artifact of that original decision?<br /> -Or was it there to be narrative connection to the &quot;Forsaken by Rome&quot; Dark Era, since this Era is also supposed to be dealing with the aftermath of the fall of Rome?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 04-19-2020, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T22:02:21-07:00","id":1383090,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d err toward the latter rather than the former, but more likely the authors just saw an opportunity to stick some extra hooks in for other games. I know I went out of my way to cram as much Werewolf, Mummy, and Hunter goodies into One Thousand and One Nightmares as I could, but that was simply because I like those games.<br /> <br /> Actually, I tried to cram in everyone, but especially those three. More Werewolf is always good, Mummy needs more shout-outs, and if the era got a third line it needed to be Hunter, but I digress...<br /> <br /> I\u2019d just chalk it up to author appeal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" tar